2_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T21:32:49-07:00","id":1325866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1325860#post1325860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've never played Bayonetta, but I understand her clothes are made from her own hair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bayonetta's style cannot be described in words, yet entire books can be written debating whether her character is sexist.<br /> <br /> Yes her clothes (and some weapons) come from her body hair. All of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T22:00:01-07:00","id":1325871,"title":"","content":"Hell, one of the most interesting online articles I've read was by <b>Liana K</b> (Canadian talk show hostess and blogger) about common critiques of sexism in gaming.<br /> <br /> Basically, her issue being that women can certainly be discriminated against but it irritated the hell out of her that some feminists attacked sex and power game fantasies as well as the kind of clothing or body types of characters. Pointing out how weird and puritanical it is to be against sexuality when expressing it is a basic right of feminism.<br /> <br /> LK being a sex positive feminism and supportive of sex work in RL as a safe option for those who like it.<br /> <br /> She took plenty of flack from certain feminists as well as misogynist gamers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T22:36:16-07:00","id":1325880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1325871#post1325871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, one of the most interesting online articles I've read was by <b>Liana K</b> (Canadian talk show hostess and blogger) about common critiques of sexism in gaming.<br /> <br /> Basically, her issue being that women can certainly be discriminated against but it irritated the hell out of her that some feminists attacked sex and power game fantasies as well as the kind of clothing or body types of characters. Pointing out how weird and puritanical it is to be against sexuality when expressing it is a basic right of feminism.<br /> <br /> LK being a sex positive feminism and supportive of sex work in RL as a safe option for those who like it.<br /> <br /> She took plenty of flack from certain feminists as well as misogynist gamers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every now and then I think back to that Dove social study that showed that the vast majority of body shaming comments against women came from other women. It would be interesting to see what percentage of &quot;outraged&quot; individuals would be classified as feeling threatened by the sexualized female characters rather than being insulted by their storyline or characterization.<br /> <br /> Of course this is complicated enough when just discussing characters and premade storylines. Where it really gets messy in translation is if you are playing a table top game where everyone plays themselves. The average male gamer playing themselves just tends to be a bit meta in their game play and revel in the idea of fixing their real life problems with in game powers. The females who did play yourself games..... well..... let's just say they had few in game inhibitions.<br /> <br /> Now does that count as self empowerment, personal experimentation, or low self esteem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T22:52:00-07:00","id":1325887,"title":"","content":"I just now realized this, but take a look at that girl's neck on page 3. Does it seem abnormally long to any of you?<br /> <br /> Maybe it's just the accessories forming an optical illusion, but that doesn't look quite right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T08:22:49-07:00","id":1325996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1325880#post1325880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every now and then I think back to that Dove social study that showed that the vast majority of body shaming comments against women came from other women. It would be interesting to see what percentage of &quot;outraged&quot; individuals would be classified as feeling threatened by the sexualized female characters rather than being insulted by their storyline or characterization.<br /> <br /> Of course this is complicated enough when just discussing characters and premade storylines. Where it really gets messy in translation is if you are playing a table top game where everyone plays themselves. The average male gamer playing themselves just tends to be a bit meta in their game play and revel in the idea of fixing their real life problems with in game powers. The females who did play yourself games..... well..... let's just say they had few in game inhibitions.<br /> <br /> Now does that count as self empowerment, personal experimentation, or low self esteem?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's best not to look too much into that.<br /> <br /> Girls just wanna have fun (at the table)<br /> <br /> Just like the boys.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T08:25:20-07:00","id":1325997,"title":"","content":"In any case, amazingly this is a good conversation with none of the usual weirdness on the internet.<br /> <br /> Here's a Liana K video on video game Sexual Objectification.<br /> <br /> It gets to the Video Game Issues at 16:00<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/PM0Pp4Ona8s?t=961\" data-code=\"PM0Pp4Ona8s\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/PM0Pp4Ona8s/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> At 19:00 you actually get a kind of funny scene that's similar to Jeanette and Therese.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-19-2019, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T12:18:58-07:00","id":1326064,"title":"","content":"I am inclined to agree with her. But at the same time I think it would be a mistake, even a severe mistake, to simply dismiss the criticisms out of hand. If some behavior offends someone, including sexual behavior, we should respect that offense and take it seriously. The same is true for depictions of women and minorities. We should listen to the people making the complaints and protesting. We should consider those protests and complaints when making our own statements in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T18:10:53-07:00","id":1326136,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326064#post1326064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am inclined to agree with her. But at the same time I think it would be a mistake, even a severe mistake, to simply dismiss the criticisms out of hand. If some behavior offends someone, including sexual behavior, we should respect that offense and take it seriously. The same is true for depictions of women and minorities. We should listen to the people making the complaints and protesting. We should consider those protests and complaints when making our own statements in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A fair point, though I often wonder if we are getting bogged down in the responses to responses, rather than dealing with root causes. If a portion of the population is offended by sexualization of inanimate objects, in truth we should be looking into how best to help those people get over their hang ups rather than constantly hand wringing over if we might offend them.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Something like 1% of the population is epileptic and of those people 3% are photosensitive epileptics. But despite what a decent sized chunk of the population that is, emergency services won't give up their flashing lights, video game designers won't restrict development, anime studios won't quit making battle scenes, etc. At most the groups will avoid a specific frequency of light pulses, but not avoid flashing in general.<br /> <br /> Instead the expectation is on the individuals who suffer from the condition to self regulate their problems with medication or actively avoid sources that would give them problems. Now seizures can produce all sorts of trauma to the body and occasionally cause fatalities under unfortunate circumstances, but the focus for dealing with it remains solely with the person who has the issue rather than the companies that make use of the technology. A warning label is considered ample enough effort to allow people to make informed decisions about such things.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Obviously Epilepsy is not an apples to apples comparison to personal views on sexualization, but it does provide an interesting counter point to the expectation of everyone else changing around the needs or trigger issues of the individual rather than the individual learning how to control such responses to stimuli.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T18:24:01-07:00","id":1326139,"title":"","content":"There is an argument that it's impossible as well as a bad idea to legislate taste.<br /> <br /> No game can be all things to all people.<br /> <br /> Some people want to play a dark and terrifying vampire game.<br /> <br /> Some people want to play Underworld with guns, leather, and swords.<br /> <br /> Some people want to play a sexy game of seduction, feeding, and decadence.<br /> <br /> Other people want politics.<br /> <br /> Can't please everyone and it's better to do one thing very well than try to do everything mediocorely.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T19:27:05-07:00","id":1326151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326136#post1326136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fair point, though I often wonder if we are getting bogged down in the responses to responses, rather than dealing with root causes.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you get to the root causes without going through the responses though?<br /> <br /> A doctor can't just ignore symptoms to focus on the disease. Besides the harm symptoms can cause, diagnosing a disease is largely predicated on studying the symptoms of it.<br /> <br /> And societal problems can't be solved by giving people pills once you figure out which ones to give.<br /> <br /> There's also a fairly direct trend of need to amass evidence to sway the social opinion of people that currently have power in an institution/industry/etc. No matter how well reasoned an argument how something is sexist/racist/etc, and even coupled with a solid theory on the root causes, we don't see things actually change. There's a need for a mass of evidence until people unaffected directly recognize they need to help change things rather than ignore it as not their problem.<br /> <br /> It's not like the people of the colonies/US didn't know slavery and denying women's suffrage were moral ills until we finally got around to legally changing things. Abolitionists and women's rights movements existed before the founding the country and fought for generations against the status quo despite the obvious immorality of the status quo.<br /> <br /> It's not a far stretch to say that televised news broadcasts were hugely important to the Civil Rights movement, because lots of &quot;good people doing nothing,&quot; had to confront their inaction when it wasn't stories, or text, but live video of black people being abused by the police for trying to have their rights respected. We needed to flood society with the truth to enact meaningful change, and even so many of the root causes remain unaddressed and when brought up solutions are deflected and dismissed because there isn't the weight to press the issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously Epilepsy is not an apples to apples comparison to personal views on sexualization, but it does provide an interesting counter point to the expectation of everyone else changing around the needs or trigger issues of the individual rather than the individual learning how to control such responses to stimuli. </div> </div> </div>I don't see how it's interesting consider how far removed they are on two major points:<br /> <br /> 1) Epilepsy is a medical condition that's a matter of bad luck to have. Being subject to discrimination by society is something other people do to you. Women don't get objectified because of bad luck on the genetic lottery, but because other human beings that have to learn how to control their own actions are objectifying them.<br /> <br /> 2) The majority of people in US society have suffered discrimination of some sort, rather than extremely rare diseases. What's a reasonable adjustment for a company to make to a product for 0.03% of the population isn't the same as what something like ~60% of the population has to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T19:31:08-07:00","id":1326154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326151#post1326151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a far stretch to say that televised news broadcasts were hugely important to the Civil Rights movement, because lots of &quot;good people doing nothing,&quot; had to confront their inaction when it wasn't stories, or text, but live video of black people being abused by the police for trying to have their rights respected. We needed to flood society with the truth to enact meaningful change, and even so many of the root causes remain unaddressed and when brought up solutions are deflected and dismissed because there isn't the weight to press the issue..</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the fact that we should also be aware that &quot;internet activism&quot; isn't necessarily the forum to do it and especially over something as ultimately inconsequential as fictional vampire sexiness levels. The Rainbow Railroad raised quite a bit of money because of the Chechnya debacle from both donators offended by the Camarilla chapter and those who were made aware of the situation because of it. Real evils and real issues.<br /> <br /> It can be a trap to essentially elevate what is merely a matter of taste and interest to fans to something that's a social ill needing to be rectified.<br /> <br /> Which it isn't and in that way lies the kind of shit that people like us went through in the 90s by &quot;certain groups&quot; fearing for our souls lest we wear black and have bad attitudes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T20:04:04-07:00","id":1326166,"title":"","content":"Getting hung up on the subject is it's own trap, because the issue isn't &quot;vampire sexiness levels,&quot; or &quot;anti-LGBTQ discrimination in Chechnya,&quot; but how those subjects are treated in our society via entertainment media expressions.<br /> <br /> Rainbow Railroad getting some donations out of that mess is a great silver lining, but things would be even better if the Chechnya section was well written as a game element and an awareness raising element; rather than it managing to raise awareness despite itself. Raising some awareness doesn't excuse the mistakes in the writing.<br /> <br /> Using &quot;taste&quot; to avoid valid criticisms isn't a good thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T20:17:25-07:00","id":1326169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326166#post1326166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting hung up on the subject is it's own trap, because the issue isn't &quot;vampire sexiness levels,&quot; or &quot;anti-LGBTQ discrimination in Chechnya,&quot; but how those subjects are treated in our society via entertainment media expressions.<br /> <br /> Rainbow Railroad getting some donations out of that mess is a great silver lining, but things would be even better if the Chechnya section was well written as a game element and an awareness raising element; rather than it managing to raise awareness despite itself. Raising some awareness doesn't excuse the mistakes in the writing.<br /> <br /> Using &quot;taste&quot; to avoid valid criticisms isn't a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taste is when something falls into an area of having both positive and negative qualities that appeal to certain segments of the public. Some things are objectively sexist (or even misogynist) but there's a lot larger area where it offends some while empowers other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T20:26:08-07:00","id":1326172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326166#post1326166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raising some awareness doesn't excuse the mistakes in the writing.<br /> <br /> Using &quot;taste&quot; to avoid valid criticisms isn't a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the first part, but am confused with the second part. If the Camarilla book had gotten the Chechnya portion right the first time - and they should have tried to get it right the firs time - the &quot;good taste&quot; issue would probably never have come up. The fact it is such a failure is why it is in such bad taste.<br /> <br /> An effort should always be made to get things right the first time. Too few people make the effort.<br /> <br /> While disappointing to some, in terms of VtM:B2, perhaps the best solutions is to down play the sexuality and sexiness.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T20:55:23-07:00","id":1326180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326151#post1326151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Epilepsy is a medical condition that's a matter of bad luck to have. Being subject to discrimination by society is something other people do to you. Women don't get objectified because of bad luck on the genetic lottery, but because other human beings that have to learn how to control their own actions are objectifying them.<br /> <br /> 2) The majority of people in US society have suffered discrimination of some sort, rather than extremely rare diseases. What's a reasonable adjustment for a company to make to a product for 0.03% of the population isn't the same as what something like ~60% of the population has to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Epilepsy can be an inherited disorder or it can be the result of brain damage from physical trauma or chemical exposure. Also for a long time epilepsy and its seizures had quite a lot of social negativity associated with it, it wasn't exactly uncommon to see epileptics being cast in a bad light by religious groups. So its not that far removed if you understand the history.<br /> <br /> As for your second point, as written it doesn't make sense to me. If the majority of people encounter discrimination, then they should be adept at dealing with the situation, like being stuck in rush hour traffic, sure its not pleasant, but not anything special either. Also just to be clear, are you claiming that 60% of people are discriminated against or just females? Because if we are using basic definition of sexism, then it would closer to 90%-95% when you really think about it. On the other hand if you are suggesting that only women can be objectified or sexually discriminated against, then that is not only blatantly untrue, but bordering closely on being a sexist view point of its own. Or did you mean something else? I just want to make sure I am understanding your position correctly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Random side thought, if Vampire is all about power fantasy and wish fulfillment, and what represents those things changes with each generation of gamers, does that mean that V6 or V7 will be about being able to hold down a job and pay the rent on time rather than sexual politics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T21:13:18-07:00","id":1326184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326172#post1326172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While disappointing to some, in terms of VtM:B2, perhaps the best solutions is to down play the sexuality and sexiness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I argue they should play it up for the heterosexual female and gay male gamers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T21:41:46-07:00","id":1326190,"title":"","content":"From my experience, it captured Los Angeles perfectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T23:47:00-07:00","id":1326205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326169#post1326169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taste is when something falls into an area of having both positive and negative qualities that appeal to certain segments of the public. Some things are objectively sexist (or even misogynist) but there's a lot larger area where it offends some while empowers other.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that this definition of taste means that objectively sexist things are still a matter of taste. After all, an objectively sexist thing empowers sexists and offends people that don't like sexism.<br /> <br /> That's the problem with using &quot;taste&quot; as you are. It doesn't account for the tastes of people with beliefs we find objectionable as a society.<br /> <br /> Trying to draw a line between &quot;matters of taste,&quot; and objectionable material doesn't work, because there are people who find objectionable material to their taste, and thus it's always going to be both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326172#post1326172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with the first part, but am confused with the second part.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second part? It's not aimed at the Camarilla book specifically. It's a more general comment that taste doesn't really justify saying that there's some sort of grey area that's just taste, because there's no way to avoid that justifying stuff that shouldn't just be a matter of taste.<br /> <br /> To an extent, I'm saying to this conversation, taste is irrelevant. Taste is just whether people like something or not, not if they find it objectionable. I don't like lots of things, but I think their existence is just fine. That's taste. Something can be to my tastes, or not, and still have enough sexist elements that I'd consider it sexist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While disappointing to some, in terms of VtM:B2, perhaps the best solutions is to down play the sexuality and sexiness. </div> </div> </div>It's a matter of execution though. Toning it down might be better if they don't want to put in the energy to execute well (which is a lot), but there's a dearth of games that actually do it well and it would be good to see more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326180#post1326180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Epilepsy can be an inherited disorder or it can be the result of brain damage from physical trauma or chemical exposure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Largely irrelevant to my point though (and only something that contradicts things I left out rather than something I said). People don't go around purposefully giving people epilepsy. People go around purposefully perpetuating discrimination in society; and unknowingly as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also for a long time epilepsy and its seizures had quite a lot of social negativity associated with it, it wasn't exactly uncommon to see epileptics being cast in a bad light by religious groups. So its not that far removed if you understand the history. </div> </div> </div>Discrimination against disabilities is something I'm intimately familiar with.<br /> <br /> Having a condition isn't the same as being discriminated against for it; and you were expressly discussing accommodations for disabilities (reducing flashes or frequencies of light used in them to avoid triggering an epileptic episode), not discrimination against them (social mistreatment of seizures was not part of your post).. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the majority of people encounter discrimination, then they should be adept at dealing with the situation, like being stuck in rush hour traffic, sure its not pleasant, but not anything special either. </div> </div> </div>The... lack of empathy here is astounding.<br /> <br /> First, that people experience discrimination doesn't meant they want to experience it more when seeking out entertainment. To use your analogy, I might be used to sitting in traffic, but I'm not going to go sit in traffic just for fun because it's a daily frustration.<br /> <br /> Second, discrimination is not some minor inconvenience. It's a traumatic experience that regardless of having successful coping mechanisms isn't something we should expect people to simply endure for the sake of other people's entertainment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also just to be clear, are you claiming that 60% of people are discriminated against or just females? </div> </div> </div>While relatively unscientific, attempts to poll all Americans on how many people feel they experience discrimination ranges from ~55% to ~85%, with more polls tending towards the low end. Of course meta-analysis is hard because phrasing, methodologies, and so on make it hard to make any sort of conclusive statement. I agree the number is probably towards the higher end in reality, but coming up with numbers to use in conversations based on something more than speculation is useful.<br /> <br /> So no, there's nothing more to try to read into it than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Random side thought, if Vampire is all about power fantasy and wish fulfillment,... </div> </div> </div>This seems a questionable premise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and what represents those things changes with each generation of gamers, does that mean that V6 or V7 will be about being able to hold down a job and pay the rent on time rather than sexual politics? </div> </div> </div>I doubt it would change much.<br /> <br /> On the &quot;jobs&quot; side of things it's worth remembering that VtM was started before the Clinton boom. The late 80s and early 90s were, like now, a period of high unemployment, low wages, and economic uncertainty for the lower and middle classes. It was a huge influence on the punk parts of the game. The whole Anarch vs. Camarilla conflict represents that; even in the Revised mode of Anarches as barely anything more than a faction within the Cam.<br /> <br /> The Cam has always been the capitalists that horde the wealth at the top and string along the lower ranks with promises of raises, promotions, and more if they just stick to the game plan. The Anarchs have always been out to reject that and try to find a different way, but are stuck in a world that doesn't really make it functional to do more than play the capitalist game.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sexual politics&quot; has been part of human discourse and entertainment for literally all of recorded history; it's not going anywhere any time soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T01:22:52-07:00","id":1326214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that this definition of taste means that objectively sexist things are still a matter of taste. After all, an objectively sexist thing empowers sexists and offends people that don't like sexism.<br /> <br /> That's the problem with using &quot;taste&quot; as you are. It doesn't account for the tastes of people with beliefs we find objectionable as a society.<br /> <br /> Trying to draw a line between &quot;matters of taste,&quot; and objectionable material doesn't work, because there are people who find objectionable material to their taste, and thus it's always going to be both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. It also can result in people oppressing women in the name of protecting them. Just because taste can be used as a defense by the people who don't deserve it, doesn't mean it's not true. History is full of people who have burned artists and destroyed art.<br /> <br /> It's an extreme example but doesn't make it less true. There needs to be freedom of expression when it offends some as offense is sometimes the only way that art can make positive contributions to society can be made (freedom of sexual expression being one of the basic rights of women in many countries that is denied). The Handmaid's Tale (literary version) talks about how the protagonist's mother's anti-obscenity crusades helped in the rise of Gilead.<br /> <br /> I admit I'm very concerned about this because I grew up in the Bible Belt and experienced some (mild) discrimination for my reading material and hobbies. I'm also a horror writer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-20-2019, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T02:29:09-07:00","id":1326224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326214#post1326214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also can result in people oppressing women in the name of protecting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does acknowledging that taste isn't a useful metric for analyzing a piece of fiction, or not allowing criticism to be tossed aside under the aegis of &quot;matters of taste,&quot; result in this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just because taste can be used as a defense by the people who don't deserve it, doesn't mean it's not true. History is full of people who have burned artists and destroyed art. </div> </div> </div>There is no logical connection between any of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There needs to be freedom of expression when it offends some as offense is sometimes the only way that art can make positive contributions to society can be made (,,,) </div> </div> </div>Nobody's talking about changing the law (at least in most Western countries, and if we are we're talking about moving the laws towards more freedom in places that don't have it).<br /> <br /> We're talking about the freedom to criticize expression. If someone writes a bunch of books with a constant message of, &quot;women can't get raped because there's not such thing as a woman that doesn't want sex from a man,&quot; the freedom to produce that doesn't in anyway protect the author from the freedom of the rest of us to call it out for being rape apologist sexist crap. It doesn't stop the freedom of stores to not carry it to avoid tarnishing their own reputations. Etc. It doesn't matter what genre the works are in, or how many copies they can sell anyway. It doesn't even matter if people are morons and buy the books just to burn them.<br /> <br /> The second artists are free from the consequences of putting out art that has negative impacts rather than positive ones, is the moment reasonable artists get drowned out by propagandists. Artists looking to push positive change with their art need us to criticize art. They need it to keep the stuff without good intentions shunned for what it is, and they need it to be kept on their own toes to make sure their intentions and ideals make it on to the page well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T02:59:20-07:00","id":1326229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326180#post1326180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random side thought, if Vampire is all about power fantasy and wish fulfillment, and what represents those things changes with each generation of gamers, does that mean that V6 or V7 will be about being able to hold down a job and pay the rent on time rather than sexual politics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, this talk of power fantasy and VtMB reminds me of the TV show <i>Jessica Jones</i>. One of the ways in which that works as a power fantasy for me is the agency that the protagonist has as a successful self-employed PI, even though most of the job itself sounds both boring and dangerous. I suppose that the equivalents in VtM are Autarkis like Beckett and Lucita.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 07-20-2019, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T06:20:10-07:00","id":1326251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326224#post1326224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're talking about the freedom to criticize expression. If someone writes a bunch of books with a constant message of, &quot;women can't get raped because there's not such thing as a woman that doesn't want sex from a man,&quot; the freedom to produce that doesn't in anyway protect the author from the freedom of the rest of us to call it out for being rape apologist sexist crap. It doesn't stop the freedom of stores to not carry it to avoid tarnishing their own reputations. Etc. It doesn't matter what genre the works are in, or how many copies they can sell anyway. It doesn't even matter if people are morons and buy the books just to burn them.<br /> <br /> The second artists are free from the consequences of putting out art that has negative impacts rather than positive ones, is the moment reasonable artists get drowned out by propagandists. Artists looking to push positive change with their art need us to criticize art. They need it to keep the stuff without good intentions shunned for what it is, and they need it to be kept on their own toes to make sure their intentions and ideals make it on to the page well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as an artist, what I'm saying is that freedom of expression of art is very important. Otherwise, even if it's just mildly changed with no legal consequences, it can just be...bland.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T12:08:13-07:00","id":1326314,"title":"","content":"There's going to be plenty of bland art anyway. Being good isn't a prerequisite for being an artists, and even great artists have flops.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the freedom of expression of criticism is a net good for the freedom of expression of art. Without criticism, art is doomed to worse than blandness.<br /> <br /> The partially antagonistic relationship between art and criticism is the avenue by which art impacts society as more than entertainment. Critical analysis is how people look at the deeper meaning of art beyond the superficial aesthetic appeal of it.<br /> <br /> And at this point, I'm really not sure what you're disagreeing with in all this. You're not actually saying anything I'm saying is wrong... you're just making some vague appeal to the idea that art is important and.... that somehow means art needs to be protected from criticism as if it was censorship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T12:42:23-07:00","id":1326322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326184#post1326184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I argue they should play it up for the heterosexual female and gay male gamers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a bi-sexual man, I don't think that would stop the game from being sexist. It would just make it an equal opportunity offender, and being sexist to men would not diminish its sexism towards women.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T12:50:14-07:00","id":1326323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326322#post1326322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking as a bi-sexual man, I don't think that would stop the game from being sexist. It would just make it an equal opportunity offender, and being sexist to men would not diminish its sexism towards women.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is catering to sexual desire a sexist thing or a natural part of humanity and the basis for much in the way of art?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T13:05:57-07:00","id":1326324,"title":"","content":"It will be both. Is it both. If even one person views something as sexist or racist, then it is racist or sexist. And that has to be taken seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T13:21:35-07:00","id":1326328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326324#post1326324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It will be both. Is it both. If even one person views something as sexist or racist, then it is racist or sexist. And that has to be taken seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but some also feel that condemning sexuality and muting it is sexist.<br /> <br /> Its why sex positive feminism exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T14:09:03-07:00","id":1326335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326324#post1326324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It will be both. Is it both. If even one person views something as sexist or racist, then it is racist or sexist. And that has to be taken seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you trying to sound ridiculous?<br /> <br /> Because that sounds really ridiculous...<br /> <br /> I could use this argument to make anything race/sexist, you'd take them all seriously?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16290-generallyconfused","name":"GenerallyConfused","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16290_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T14:13:18-07:00","id":1326337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326324#post1326324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It will be both. Is it both. If even one person views something as sexist or racist, then it is racist or sexist. And that has to be taken seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>This... doesn't seem a useful way to doing things.<br /> <br /> We should take critical statements of sexism and racism seriously, even if by what seems like a tiny minority of people. But taking it seriously doesn't mean accepting it as a functional assessment of something without critical analysis to go along with it.<br /> <br /> Otherwise these terms lose meaning. If anyone calling something sexist makes it sexist, than sexism because a hollow term without meaning because everything is sexist and nothing is sexist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T14:24:56-07:00","id":1326341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326322#post1326322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as a bi-sexual man, I don't think that would stop the game from being sexist. It would just make it an equal opportunity offender, and being sexist to men would not diminish its sexism towards women.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also speaking as a bi man, surely sexism involves one sex (or gender) getting better or worse treatment than another? The problems I saw in Bloodlines were what fuzzball6846 summarized on the first page: the female characters being for the most part sexualized, and the male characters not. If the writers of BL2 want to play up the sexual themes that, let's face it, have always existed in Vampire, and do it equally to both genders (e.g. including some male NPCs with revealing outfits and Seduction dialogue), I see no problem with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T15:08:38-07:00","id":1326350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326337#post1326337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This... doesn't seem a useful way to doing things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking it seriously is what it means to listen to people who make allegations of sexism and racism. It means respecting the people make allegations and taking the statement and using them to guide work in the future.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T15:10:18-07:00","id":1326351,"title":"","content":"I think it's still a matter of execution. Objectifying everyone isn't really a great option just to avoid objectifying some people.<br /> <br /> If BL2 just increases the number of Romeros and Chucks out there to interact with (even if prettier ones), it's not really addressing the underlying issue in BL1 (which is more than it sets up a decent premise for social commentary around sexism and then never executes on it, so the sexism is just sorta sitting there instead of being part of the social commentary of the game).<br /> <br /> If BL2 is going to keep intimacy options (I don't really think BL1 has much in the way of romance in the way it's usually used in video-games) on par with BL1, wider variety of options would be good, but it should be at least coupled with a bit less sexism sitting around with commentary. To go back to a previous analogy, BL2 doesn't need to add in traffic jams just because they're part of reality; it's just frustration if there's no pay off in the game itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T15:11:38-07:00","id":1326353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326350#post1326350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Taking it seriously is what it means to listen to people who make allegations of sexism and racism. It means respecting the people make allegations and taking the statement and using them to guide work in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I agree with that. It's combining it with, &quot;If even one person views something as sexist or racist, then it is racist or sexist.&quot; that doesn't really work for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T15:19:01-07:00","id":1326354,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to point out that depiction of sexuality and sex does not necessarily mean sexism. Which is that the act of physically presenting sexually desirable NPCs and even making them able to be flirted with or fed on/sexually interacted with as part of the vampire fantasy does not in any way necessarily degrade one gender or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T15:48:36-07:00","id":1326356,"title":"","content":"And I'll point out, again, that execution matters. The problems in BL1 aren't that it has sexy vampires, but what it does with them (or in my view what it doesn't do with them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T15:55:20-07:00","id":1326358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326356#post1326356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'll point out, again, that execution matters. The problems in BL1 aren't that it has sexy vampires, but what it does with them (or in my view what it doesn't do with them).</div> </div> </div> </div>I am interested what you'd prefer they do with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T18:16:26-07:00","id":1326378,"title":"","content":"In general? Something besides being sexy.<br /> <br /> Yes, plenty of them are involved in the plot, but that largely steals their agency and gives it to the player. Jeannette never learns how to turn her rebellious sexuality into something more thoughtfully in-line with sex positive feminism without the player's intervention. And at that point her involvement in the story ends and we never see what happens next for her. Vivi and Damsel are just quest givers; Vivi even worse as she's supposed to be the Toreador Primogen but that's a joke because of Issac so all she actually does is keep her herd safe. Ash and Isaac if we want to look at the other side of things are too wrapped up in their own heads to really have any potential sexual messages work.<br /> <br /> Basically, if BL1 was trying to promote the idea of sex positive feminism, it stopped at pointing out that prudishness is dumb, without ever making the case for the alternative being good. None of the characters who are actual major players in the story are part of this messaging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T19:00:46-07:00","id":1326386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326378#post1326378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general? Something besides being sexy.<br /> <br /> Yes, plenty of them are involved in the plot, but that largely steals their agency and gives it to the player. Jeannette never learns how to turn her rebellious sexuality into something more thoughtfully in-line with sex positive feminism without the player's intervention. And at that point her involvement in the story ends and we never see what happens next for her. Vivi and Damsel are just quest givers; Vivi even worse as she's supposed to be the Toreador Primogen but that's a joke because of Issac so all she actually does is keep her herd safe. Ash and Isaac if we want to look at the other side of things are too wrapped up in their own heads to really have any potential sexual messages work.<br /> <br /> Basically, if BL1 was trying to promote the idea of sex positive feminism, it stopped at pointing out that prudishness is dumb, without ever making the case for the alternative being good. None of the characters who are actual major players in the story are part of this messaging.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vivi being the Primogen isn't true I believe because she's allied with Isaac.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T01:24:27-07:00","id":1326420,"title":"","content":"OK, minor nitpick accepted... though that adds to a different issue in that the only named women in positions in power in the game are Terese/Jeannette, which is meaningless because they're the biggest fish in a pond that they make up half of and they have no actual power as everyone else basically walks all over their claim, and Ming.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T04:47:33-07:00","id":1326443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326420#post1326420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, minor nitpick accepted... though that adds to a different issue in that the only named women in positions in power in the game are Terese/Jeannette, which is meaningless because they're the biggest fish in a pond that they make up half of and they have no actual power as everyone else basically walks all over their claim, and Ming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ming Xiao being the second half of the villains and her being ruler of Chinatown means that the rulers of two regions in the game are female. That's not insignificant.<br /> <br /> And there's not that many Kindred in the game period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T05:24:56-07:00","id":1326450,"title":"","content":"I addressed why Therese/Jeanette's leadership of Santa Monica shouldn't really count as being significant.<br /> <br /> And there are ~30 vampires in the game that are either named or significant despite not having a name (like the Sheriff). And I'm not counting the thin-bloods at the beach if you wanted to tack on some more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T06:17:27-07:00","id":1326455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fuzzball6846</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1325416#post1325416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't consider Bloodlines to be sexist, it's not wrong to call it a &amp;quot;male power fantasy&amp;quot;. Most video games, especially ones about vampires or other supernatural creatures, are power fantasies. That's the point. Being a reality-bending, superhuman creature is the definition of a power fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an issue with Bloodlines trying to appeal to a broader audience by reducing the source material to a shallow power fantasy. If it was any faithful to the source material it would be different, having to suffer the consequences and question the morality of your actions is the antithesis of power fantasy, and the tabletop is all about that. Unfortunately the mainstream gaming community arent ready for that sort of introspective story (and with the way things are going I doubt they will ever be at all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T09:28:00-07:00","id":1326474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326450#post1326450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I addressed why Therese/Jeanette's leadership of Santa Monica shouldn't really count as being significant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree.<br /> <br /> * La Croix and Therese are allied<br /> * Tung is in hiding because of Therese<br /> * The Thin Bloods are terrified of the authority in the area<br /> <br /> We also see Therese's big business project in the Hotel, the Club, and her Blood Bank.<br /> <br /> She's a powerful figure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326455#post1326455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an issue with Bloodlines trying to appeal to a broader audience by reducing the source material to a shallow power fantasy. If it was any faithful to the source material it would be different, having to suffer the consequences and question the morality of your actions is the antithesis of power fantasy, and the tabletop is all about that. Unfortunately the mainstream gaming community arent ready for that sort of introspective story (and with the way things are going I doubt they will ever be at all).</div> </div> </div> </div>I remind you that Vampire: The Masquerade is the inspiration for Underworld and known as the <b>Trenchcoats and Katana</b> game.<br /> <br /> It's always been about the duality of the horror versus the awesomeness of the power.<br /> <br /> And Bloodlines has many-many moral choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T09:45:56-07:00","id":1326480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326474#post1326474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * La Croix and Therese are allied</div> </div> </div> </div>More than just allies... Apparently Lacroix was &quot;riding Jeanette's pogo stick&quot; if I remember the phrase correctly...<br /> <br /> Yes, Jeanette was pegging Lacroix's ass... this is canon to the lore... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T09:48:22-07:00","id":1326481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326480#post1326480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More than just allies... Apparently Lacroix was &quot;riding Jeanette's pogo stick&quot; if I remember the phrase correctly...<br /> <br /> Yes, Jeanette was pegging Lacroix's ass... this is canon to the lore... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I don't recall that.<br /> <br /> I was thinking about the fact that Therese and he were running the fake art gallery of Cainite art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T10:21:30-07:00","id":1326488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326481#post1326481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, I don't recall that.<br /> <br /> I was thinking about the fact that Therese and he were running the fake art gallery of Cainite art.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It wasn't explicitly stated in the game itself, but I believe it was revealed in one of the books that Lacroix and Jeanette were in bed together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T13:03:35-07:00","id":1326511,"title":"","content":"OK, first off, is there are real point here, or are you just trying to turn this into a nitpick off as it if actually undermines the point I made that started all this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326474#post1326474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Name one thing she actually did that wouldn't have made her a glorified Keeper of Elysium if her club and the blood bank were in someone else's domain instead of being in a place where none of the vampires care enough to take it over?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's always been about the duality of the horror versus the awesomeness of the power. </div> </div> </div>The authorial intent has always been the horror of power (this goes back to that whole &quot;did you just put in an element, or did you actually use it,&quot; thing). That that the audience chooses to engage with it in different modes is a somewhat different conversation about how authorial intent and audience interpretation should be weighed in critical analysis.<br /> <br /> There's a reason Requiem and V5 both moved to put some mechanical roadblocks to have the games work well as pure power fantasy as written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Bloodlines has many-many moral choices. </div> </div> </div>How many of them actually matter besides keeping your Humanity meter up without spending XP on it?<br /> <br /> You don't need to act consistently moral, just moral enough times to make sure your Humanity doesn't drop for the times your moral choices actually drop it (which is probably less than it should if we were actually trying to make a point about morality in the game).<br /> <br /> I've never dropped below Humanity 5 in Bloodlines... despite all the murder, theft, and just generally not being a good person my characters have done. You actively have to try to put your Humanity at risk in the game.<br /> <br /> And beyond that there's so few choices with consequences. One of the first things you can do in the game is shake down a rich guy for cash and vendor trash... and nothing happens to you if you do it. And that's how most of the game works. It's pretty simple why that's the case: avoiding dead ends in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T14:04:11-07:00","id":1326524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326511#post1326511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Name one thing she actually did that wouldn't have made her a glorified Keeper of Elysium if her club and the blood bank were in someone else's domain instead of being in a place where none of the vampires care enough to take it over?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with santa monica, but the pier is an attraction that attracts visitors (from the pictures I got from google),<br /> this means a prime feeding ground (at least, if it weren't for the murder that happened there, and the boat incident),<br /> <br /> if Therese holds the domain, vampires who go there have to go through her<br /> <br /> she was also restoring a resort (the haunted one), and trying to set up art galleries (which are good points to the Toreador),<br /> she was only on the early phases of her projects, but she was on the right path<br /> <br /> plus, as we learn later, Camarilla had little substantial claim in the state, they needed as much territory as they could get (and santa monica was no exception),<br /> hell, even the sabbat had an absurdly large depot of weaponry there<br /> <br /> PS: I'm not challenging any of your earlier points, just talking","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 07-21-2019, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T14:04:48-07:00","id":1326525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326511#post1326511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've never dropped below Humanity 5 in Bloodlines... despite all the murder, theft, and just generally not being a good person my characters have done. You actively have to try to put your Humanity at risk in the game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the process would seem to be modding the game. I never dropped below 3 Humanity with any other clan than Toreador, even when I decided to go on a mass murder spree and slaughter dozens of cops and citizens in the streets. Seems you need to do some really dark shit to hit Wassail, and Bloodlines 1 wasn't programmed with those options available to the player. The only reason I got so low with Toreador is because the humanity shifts were worth double the usual dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T14:50:29-07:00","id":1326533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326524#post1326524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not familiar with santa monica, but the pier is an attraction that attracts visitors (from the pictures I got from google),<br /> this means a prime feeding ground (at least, if it weren't for the murder that happened there, and the boat incident),</div> </div> </div> </div>In reality? Absolutely. In the game itself, Santa Monica is treated as turd of a territory. Before the PC moves in, Therese, Jeannette, and Tung are the only acknowledged vampires living there with a small band of thin-bloods hiding there because it's so devoid of vampires compared to LA.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if Therese holds the domain, vampires who go there have to go through her </div> </div> </div>Supposedly? But it's clearly not the case. The Kuei-jin, Sabbat, and the Southland Slasher all have a presences there despite her claim. LaCroix floods her domain with vampires trying to kill you and no matter how good your relationship with her, she can't do anything about it.<br /> <br /> It seems pretty clear her claim is in-name only with LaCroix and Issac treating it as something they have the actual final say over instead of Therese/Jeanette.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> she was also restoring a resort (the haunted one), and trying to set up art galleries (which are good points to the Toreador),<br /> she was only on the early phases of her projects, but she was on the right path </div> </div> </div>This is Keeper of Elysium work, not the work of a Prince/Baron.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> plus, as we learn later, Camarilla had little substantial claim in the state, they needed as much territory as they could get (and santa monica was no exception), </div> </div> </div>Therese/Jeanette are playing both sides there, with Therese seeking alliance with the Camarilla while Jeanette sides with the Anarchs. Therese also considers herself the Baron of Santa Monica, not the Prince, with means - at least before LaCroix tried to move in and take over - she was part of the Anarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T16:10:05-07:00","id":1326551,"title":"","content":"err... can't argue with any of that :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T16:14:53-07:00","id":1326553,"title":"","content":"I can. The idea Santa Monica is a turd of the game and there's only 3 vampires there is like arguing that Whiterun in Skyrim is just a Blacksmithery, Castle, and Alehouse.<br /> <br /> There's limitations of the medium.<br /> <br /> Just because you don't meet any of the other vampires in Santa Monica doesn't mean they don't exist.<br /> <br /> Obviously SOMEONE embraced that Gangrel serial killer.<br /> <br /> By this logic, there's only 6 Anarchs in all of Los Angeles (Nines, Skelter, Damsel, Isaac, Vivi, and Smiling Jack)<br /> <br /> As we see with the Blood Hunt at the end of the game, there's a lot of other vampires in Los Angeles hunting you. Almost a dozen in Santa Monica alone, you just never learn their name because they're trying to diablerize you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-21-2019, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T16:40:38-07:00","id":1326555,"title":"","content":"I've replayed Bloodlines with a female character recently, having played it with male characters before. It really does become obvious, when you do it, that the game was written for straight men. Nobody who created it went &quot;Mwahahahaha, I hate those women so much&quot;, which some seem to imply is a requirement for sexism. But it very consistently caters to the straight male experience, introducing elements (considered to be) pleasing to us and avoiding those that aren't. Like most gaming, or media in general, back in 2004. There's no point in denying it or taking it as some sort of condemnation or attack, we just need to expect today's media to do better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T17:09:34-07:00","id":1326559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326553#post1326553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's limitations of the medium.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are limits. Bloodlines was a few miles away on the 'safe' side of things. It in no way pushed the limits of the medium at the time.<br /> <br /> First off, Tung makes it clear that Santa Monica being a turd is an in-character impression at least he has. So this isn't just an impression created by any technological issues, but something made a case for in the script itself.<br /> <br /> Second, nothing with the technology of the time stopped the game from having some non-interactive named vampire NPCs milling around. If they wanted Santa Monica to look more populated they could have. You don't have to flood the game or anything, but there's lots of little touches you can do. A vampire at the club besides Therese/Jeanette. A Nos in the sewers later in the plot once the Nose don't feel as threatened by the Sabbat. A vampire stalking the pier that mutters something about being bored watching the Thin-Bloods for a reason to do something to them once the pier area is open. Have Jack, Therese/Jeanette, and Tung mention vampires (you can hack Therese's and Jeanette's computers which would have been a perfect time to add some random vampires to the setting with minimal work) that you never actually see because they don't matter to the story.<br /> <br /> Those are the exact tricks TES series uses to make their cities seem more populated than they really are. Seyda Neen, the starting town in Morrowind (which came out before Bloodlines) has over 25 <b>named</b> characters around. Most of them are set dressing, but it makes the tiny little place look populated.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines didn't need the breadth of Morrowind, but Morrowind more than adequately shows that any appeal to limitations is nonsense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T17:26:56-07:00","id":1326561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326553#post1326553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can. The idea Santa Monica is a turd of the game and there's only 3 vampires there is like arguing that Whiterun in Skyrim is just a Blacksmithery, Castle, and Alehouse.<br /> <br /> There's limitations of the medium.<br /> <br /> Just because you don't meet any of the other vampires in Santa Monica doesn't mean they don't exist.<br /> <br /> Obviously SOMEONE embraced that Gangrel serial killer.<br /> <br /> By this logic, there's only 6 Anarchs in all of Los Angeles (Nines, Skelter, Damsel, Isaac, Vivi, and Smiling Jack)<br /> <br /> As we see with the Blood Hunt at the end of the game, there's a lot of other vampires in Los Angeles hunting you. Almost a dozen in Santa Monica alone, you just never learn their name because they're trying to diablerize you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Betram outright states <i>&quot;there's only like 3 vampires in all of Santa Monica... pfft, some kingdom!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Also, just because that Gangrel was in the area, doesn't mean he came from there (remember, Gangrel are drifters). He was chasing after the ones who killed his family, and even goes so far as to run over to Downtown, as well as Hollywood. By the time you finally track him back to the junkyard, he's ready to leave the city. As you find out, if you choose to spare his life.<br /> <br /> And on another point, that Gangrel was both a caitiff, and a habitual Masquerade violator. Even if she did take over, she would need to dispose of him as quickly as possible, or else her ability to control the domain would have been called into question.<br /> <br /> Final point, and this is most important, is the fact that Therese and Jeanette were ideologically opposed to one another. Even if Therese did begin making headway into establishing order and authority, it would not be long before Jeanette started to undermine her efforts. Combine this with the fact they are both the same person, and we can assume that Therese's effectiveness as Baron / Prince would have slowed to a crawl, if not a complete standstill. Even if you do kill Jeanette, the fact that her insanity is INCURABLE, probably means that she would manifest herself again in the future, or else Therese would develop a new personality, one who might have been just as bad, or even worse than her previous one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T18:29:18-07:00","id":1326571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Do you think that bloodlines was, in any way, a sexist game?</span></b><br /> </div> </div> </div>Going to say no, because I've never looked at a piece of media and thought that. From articles and the like recently, I'm very grateful that I don't. Perhaps if I went looking I might, but I would rather judge thing on how much I liked them and not if someone somewhere might not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24824-notempathic","name":"NotEmpathic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T18:44:27-07:00","id":1326574,"title":"","content":"&quot;It's not sexist because I don't care if it is,&quot; is horrible. Besides any moral or ethic cases, I'll make a direct appeal to self-interest:<br /> <br /> Not caring about how other people feel about a game/etc. enables companies to not care about minority voices. Not being cared about drives minority voices out of the game from fans to creative talent. Less fans of what you like means it's less profitable and it's harder for more of what you like to get made. Less creative diversity means less ideas coming to the table, and you just get the same products over and over.<br /> <br /> Care, because it's actually better for your life in the long run to care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T19:08:50-07:00","id":1326575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326574#post1326574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It's not sexist because I don't care if it is,&quot; is horrible. Besides any moral or ethic cases, I'll make a direct appeal to self-interest:<br /> <br /> Not caring about how other people feel about a game/etc. enables companies to not care about minority voices. Not being cared about drives minority voices out of the game from fans to creative talent. Less fans of what you like means it's less profitable and it's harder for more of what you like to get made. Less creative diversity means less ideas coming to the table, and you just get the same products over and over.<br /> <br /> Care, because it's actually better for your life in the long run to care.</div> </div> </div> </div>Evidence suggests otherwise. And it's not like my opinion actually matters, deliberately avoiding looking through any lens beyond &quot;is this good/fun&quot;. Just felt depressed by the thread and wanted to give a little voice to anyone who just doesn't care","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24824-notempathic","name":"NotEmpathic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T19:44:25-07:00","id":1326582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NotEmpathic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326575#post1326575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evidence suggests otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>What evidence are you referring to?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...wanted to give a little voice to anyone who just doesn't care </div> </div> </div>On forums, the generally accepted away to express disinterest in a topic is to not participate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T19:52:56-07:00","id":1326586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evidence suggests that &quot;who just doesn't care.&quot; people contribute to a status quo, which in terms of gaming has decidedly had problems with sexism in gaming. Honestly, the only reason a person really has to post that sort of apathy is as a, at best, passive way of telling people who are saying examining the issue in games need to keep quiet. It's a person who has taken a side's cop out from actually acknowledging that they have in fact, taken a side.<br /> <br /> Yeah no thanks. I like good games, and taking games seriously and examining issues of sexism in games ultimately helps make for better games in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, your take on it resonates strongly with an <i>&quot;us vs them&quot;</i> sort of mentality, and those almost never end well. I mean, you practically said that anybody who doesn't openly criticize such things in the media is part of the problem.<br /> <br /> It's not that people don't care about the issues, it's that addressing those issues in a format that is primarily supposed to be used for entertainment is the wrong way to go about it. There is an overwhelming amount of evidence to support this. Just take a look at any form of modern media, which tried to <i>&quot;get woke&quot;</i> as the saying goes now. Virtually every single one of them have crashed and burned within weeks of their initial release!<br /> <br /> People don't buy games, watch movies, or read comics to hear others spout their political driven rhetoric. They visit those things to relax and have a good time. And if you come to the party with the idea that you can use them as a medium to sway people to your ideology, you're going to find a lot of people getting pissed at you, because that's not what they paid money for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T20:19:20-07:00","id":1326591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326582#post1326582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> On forums, the generally accepted away to express disinterest in a topic is to not participate.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the kind of behavior that leads to echo chambers though.<br /> <br /> All the over reaction/correction to these kinds of questions seems to lead to bad products, not good ones.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24824-notempathic","name":"NotEmpathic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T22:09:44-07:00","id":1326616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326586#post1326586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you practically said that anybody who doesn't openly criticize such things in the media is part of the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>To paraphrase the saying: the only way to keep evil from continuing in our media, is for good people to say nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not that people don't care about the issues, it's that addressing those issues in a format that is primarily supposed to be used for entertainment is the wrong way to go about it. </div> </div> </div>Entertainment has been a primary use of artistic expression for political ends for all of human history. It's hard to get people to listen if you can't hook them in first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is an overwhelming amount of evidence to support this. </div> </div> </div>Such as?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just take a look at any form of modern media, which tried to <i>&quot;get woke&quot;</i> as the saying goes now. Virtually every single one of them have crashed and burned within weeks of their initial release! </div> </div> </div>This is hardly true as a universal statement.<br /> <br /> As well, modern media consumers are fairly keen on performative allies. That is, we see people that are being supportive not to actually be supportive, but for getting as much credit as possible for minimal actual expended effort doing the hard work. People that care see the lack of forward motion from such weak support, and non-supporters see it for the token and dishonest effort it is.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure Spike Lee, Ryan Coolger, Jordan Peele, Taika Waititi, and so on would love tell you about how badly their work bombs for their &quot;wokeness.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is one of the reasons people advocating on such things put so much stress on creative talent diversity rather than surface representation. Creative talent diversity creates more stories that resonate with people for their basis actual lived experiences rather than outsiders trying to right about stuff they know about; even if the intentions are good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People don't buy games, watch movies, or read comics to hear others spout their political driven rhetoric. </div> </div> </div>The number of successful and overtly political media out there doesn't really support this. People go to Hamilton to be entertained, but also for the politics.<br /> <br /> The problem is when the politics overtly challenges people instead of affirming their beliefs. This can be done, but it's hard and fails far more often than it succeeds. People don't feel that entertainment is spouting political driven rhetoric if that's already what they believe in, even if that's what they're watching. Challenging people too directly does tend to turn them off. Those there needs a skilled and nuanced hand that advocates a political position without being &quot;preachy.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T22:29:47-07:00","id":1326618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326616#post1326616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Entertainment has been a primary use of artistic expression for political ends for all of human history. It's hard to get people to listen if you can't hook them in first.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While this is true, and there are many stories out there which had political undertones and became hugely successful, the difference between then and now is how they portrayed their message in a much more subtle art style than waving it around in people's faces and beating them over the head with it. It's been many years since I've written any stories, fanfiction or otherwise, but even I still remember one of the core tenets of good story telling: <i>Show, Don't Tell!</i><br /> <br /> Ripli, from the Aliens franchise is a strong, independent female. But at no point in the movie does anybody come right out and state as such to the audience. Instead of telling people that Ripli is a strong character, it shows us that she's a strong character. And it does so in such a fashion that doesn't portray her as being a Marry Sue... except for Alien Resurrection, but we probably don't count that one.<br /> <br /> If the purpose of the medium is to be artistic, then the art is what you should focus on first and foremost. If the purpose of the medium is to be political, then don't insult the viewer's intelligence by claiming it's something else. Nobody is falling for that crap, and the franchises which were under the impression to the contrary are finally realizing their mistake and dialing back on the ham fisted politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T22:45:27-07:00","id":1326620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326616#post1326616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Such as?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Battlefield 5<br /> <br /> Star Wars, the new Trilogy<br /> <br /> The Captain Marvel movie<br /> <br /> Mass Effect Andromeda<br /> <br /> Marvel Comics<br /> <br /> Disney<br /> <br /> These are just ones I was able to come up with off the top of my head. The moment they started to sacrifice good story telling for shoehorning their political ideologies into the setting, they started to lose money BIG TIME. And it was only after some of these companies realized <i>&quot;alright, nobody wants this crap, let's go back to what we were doing before&quot;</i> that they finally started to see their finances recover.<br /> <br /> Maybe you haven't heard the trending phrase going around, yet?<i> &quot;Get woke, go broke.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T01:32:51-07:00","id":1326643,"title":"","content":"How on earth is &quot;let's make it so the game that doesn't assume it'll be played by a straight man&quot; even a political or controversial statement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T01:46:17-07:00","id":1326644,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326620#post1326620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Battlefield 5<br /> <br /> Star Wars, the new Trilogy<br /> <br /> The Captain Marvel movie<br /> <br /> Mass Effect Andromeda<br /> <br /> Marvel Comics<br /> <br /> Disney<br /> <br /> These are just ones I was able to come up with off the top of my head. The moment they started to sacrifice good story telling for shoehorning their political ideologies into the setting, they started to lose money BIG TIME. And it was only after some of these companies realized <i>&quot;alright, nobody wants this crap, let's go back to what we were doing before&quot;</i> that they finally started to see their finances recover.<br /> <br /> Maybe you haven't heard the trending phrase going around, yet?<i> &quot;Get woke, go broke.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ehm... sorry but do you know what you are talking about?<br /> <br /> <br /> Star Wars the new Trilogy is one of the biggest commercial hit Disney ever had,<br /> <br /> <br /> The Last Jedi made 1.3 billions at the box office<br /> And The Force Awakens 2 billions.<br /> <br /> <br /> while<br /> <br /> The Phantom Menace 1 billion<br /> The Attack of the Clones made 650 millions<br /> Revenge of the Sith made 850 millions<br /> <br /> <br /> Which means that with only 2 films out they almost surpassed the whole second trilogy.<br /> <br /> The Force Awakens isthe biggest hit in the star wars story, and The Last Jedi is the second one.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you take in account the revenue produced by the 4 star wars film we had since the start of the new trilogy (Force Awakens, Rogue One, Solo and Last Jedi) you have a marvelous revenue of 4.8 billions of dollars (4 film) compared to the 4.3 billions generated by every film since a New Hope to the Revenge of the Sith , which means that Disney has made in 4 years more profit than Lucas did in 28.<br /> <br /> Average revenue for the Disney era films is 1.2 billions, against the 843 millions for the second trilogy and the 630 per film of the original trilogy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Captain Marvel's movie made 1.12 billions at the box office and is currently the second highest grossing film of the year, and the 9th Marvel movie by revenue (oh and the 5th is the &quot;woke&quot; Black Panther)<br /> <br /> Only the 4 Avengers movie, Black Panther, Civil War and Iron Man 3 made more money than Captain Marvel.<br /> Captain Marvel made more money than Iron Man 1 and two combined, or Thor 1 and 2 combined and so on.<br /> <br /> Taking in account every Disney film since ever, Captain Marvel is the 13 highest grossin film in Disney's history, and Black Panther is the 5th.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Disney has been a colossus on the rise since EVER, and it has never &quot;gone broke&quot;.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/disneynews.us/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/Disney-Annual-Income-in-billions-1.png?resize=641%2C371&amp;ssl=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Disney's profits are rising steadily since 2009<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for Andromeda? A bugfest rushed during development with such great technical issues it became a meme. Andromeda didn't went down because it was &quot;woke&quot;, it went down because bioware has died of starvation and deadlines.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Get out from 4chan, that's not the real world, and buy the Financial Times, the Economist or some serious shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 07-22-2019, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T01:52:34-07:00","id":1326645,"title":"","content":"&quot;Get woke, go broke&quot; isn't a &quot;trending&quot; phrase among anyone other than people trying to disparage the very idea of diversity and defend the status quo. Acting like Disney is &quot;woke&quot; and acting on some kind of political agenda is hilarious, anyway. They're very carefully doing the absolute bare minimum in terms of diversity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","user":"Morty","date":". 07-22-2019, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T02:01:00-07:00","id":1326646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326474#post1326474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree.<br /> <br /> * La Croix and Therese are allied<br /> * Tung is in hiding because of Therese<br /> * The Thin Bloods are terrified of the authority in the area<br /> <br /> We also see Therese's big business project in the Hotel, the Club, and her Blood Bank.<br /> <br /> She's a powerful figure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I remind you that Vampire: The Masquerade is the inspiration for Underworld and known as the <b>Trenchcoats and Katana</b> game.<br /> <br /> It's always been about the duality of the horror versus the awesomeness of the power.<br /> <br /> And Bloodlines has many-many moral choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, safe and shallow moral choices that has little to none personal horror elements in fear of soiling the player's escapist power fantasy. Thank you, next.<br /> <br /> When the video game adaptation actually focuses on the horror rather &quot;kewl vampire powers&quot; and makes a sliver of an effort to be close to the source material in a way that is not skin deep, you can call me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T02:01:40-07:00","id":1326647,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I can't immagine the pain Disney had to suffer these last years for its choice to go woke! <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.statista.com/graphic/1/187329/box-office-revenue-of-disney-in-north-america-since-2000.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh the sacrifice made on the altar of wokeness! Alas poor Walt Disney! I knew him well!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T02:02:40-07:00","id":1326648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326645#post1326645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Get woke, go broke&amp;quot; isn't a &amp;quot;trending&amp;quot; phrase among anyone other than people trying to disparage the very idea of diversity and defend the status quo. Acting like Disney is &amp;quot;woke&amp;quot; and acting on some kind of political agenda is hilarious, anyway. They're very carefully doing the absolute bare minimum in terms of diversity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let them think that they are right, the more delusional they are the less likely it is for them to go on a rampage to try to &quot;fix&quot; the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T02:07:05-07:00","id":1326651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326511#post1326511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The authorial intent has always been the horror of power (this goes back to that whole &quot;did you just put in an element, or did you actually use it,&quot; thing). That that the audience chooses to engage with it in different modes is a somewhat different conversation about how authorial intent and audience interpretation should be weighed in critical analysis.<br /> <br /> There's a reason Requiem and V5 both moved to put some mechanical roadblocks to have the games work well as pure power fantasy as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excuse me? Requiem and V5 did the exact opposite of that. They actually made the mechanics more in tune with the personal horror themes. I dont understand why the direct media adaptation of Vampire wouldn't try to be faithful to the source material, why they need to make it into a shallow power fantasy. They probably lack artistic integrity and has their eyes on the money maker, which is that lifeless gamers want an empty escape from their lives than engage any thoughtful or mind provoking themes. Video games are the death of art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","user":"Shawarbaaz","date":". 07-22-2019, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T02:35:23-07:00","id":1326652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326618#post1326618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">..the difference between then and now is how they portrayed their message in a much more subtle art style than waving it around in people's faces and beating them over the head with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you need to bone up on your classical Greek plays. Or was Aristophanes subtle somehow?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Show, Don't Tell! </div> </div> </div>Which is entirely different from being subtle or not. And remember I'm the one that's been going on about execution rather than topic this whole time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the purpose of the medium is to be artistic, then the art is what you should focus on first and foremost. </div> </div> </div>And one of the defining aspects of art is communication. Art is a conversation between the artist and the audience. The artist needs to think about what they say and how. And that message is always going to be political in some way, because humans are political creatures.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Battlefield 5 </div> </div> </div>Was generally well reviewed, the inclusion of female character complaints amounted to nothing, and the mediocre financial successes is based on the lackluster multiplayer offerings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Star Wars, the new Trilogy </div> </div> </div>The 4th and 12th highest grossing movies of all time are evidence of things crashing and burning?<br /> <br /> Even with all the controversies the new SW trilogy has been wildly successful, with zero evidence of the online outrage impact people going to see the movies. Meta-analysis actually shows that most of the fan backlash against TLJ was based on it not following people's head canons more than anything else. So it's not about how &quot;woke&quot; they were, but that fans got so attached to how they thought things were going to happen that - after complaining TFA was too predictable - they got angry went in a different direction than predicted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Captain Marvel movie </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes, the 22nd highest grossing film of all time! So unpopular.<br /> <br /> While perhaps a bit disappointing in the reviews, it's nothing to do with &quot;wokeness.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, with SW and Captain Marvel.... Disney is clearly doing so poorly that they... just announced that Thor 4 would have Jane Foster as Thor despite all the controversies around that arc in the comics... because these movies are making billions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mass Effect Andromeda </div> </div> </div>What is this even doing on this list? Andromeda was a mediocre entry in the series for being mediocre... it didn't do anything &quot;woke.&quot; It was pretty tame in those regards to the original ME series.<br /> <br /> Or is BioWare defending their employee from attacks that were out of bounds on their face... and even worse aimed at a woman that wasn't responsible for the work being attacked... somehow something that's bad?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Marvel Comics </div> </div> </div>Their &quot;wokeness&quot; is horribly performative; at least at the top. But that's not their financial problem. The problem is their senior staff's horrible IP management that sabotages both normal &quot;mainstream&quot; titles and more diverse titles alike.<br /> <br /> People that actually look at this stuff all find the same real issue:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://screenrant.com/marvel-diversity-comic-sales-single-issue/\" target=\"_blank\">https://screenrant.com/marvel-divers...-single-issue/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.theatlantic.com/entertainment/archive/2017/05/the-real-reasons-for-marvel-comics-woes/527127/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.theatlantic.com/entertai...s-woes/527127/</a><br /> <br /> Marvel is killing itself through dumb business practices, not content. Of course, your claim was &quot;Virtually every single one of them have crashed and burned within weeks of their initial release!&quot; and Marvel is still kicking.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that Marvel put itself on the map in the Silver Age by being overtly political. All the big Marvel titles (X-men franchise being the most cited example) were all about pushing diversity. So that's half a century of crashing and burning, not a few weeks apparently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Disney </div> </div> </div>Disney is doing great financially...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These are just ones I was able to come up with off the top of my head. The moment they started to sacrifice good story telling for shoehorning their political ideologies into the setting, they started to lose money BIG TIME. And it was only after some of these companies realized <i>&quot;alright, nobody wants this crap, let's go back to what we were doing before&quot;</i> that they finally started to see their finances recover. </div> </div> </div>That's not true for any of these examples.<br /> <br /> Disney, leveraging SW and the MCU, has seen constant increase in profits for the past 15 years (longer if not for a singular bump in 2002). They have <b>half</b> of the top 25 highest grossing films of all time at the moment and only three of those movies aren't SW or MCU.<br /> <br /> BioWare and EA are not struggling financially.<br /> <br /> The BioWare, EA, and Marvel Comics examples are also completely devoid of any historical context for those franchises or companies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe you haven't heard the trending phrase going around, yet?<i> &quot;Get woke, go broke.&quot;</i> </div> </div> </div>Internet buzzwords aren't truth. All the facts point in the exact opposite direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 07-22-2019, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T02:53:30-07:00","id":1326654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326643#post1326643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How on earth is &quot;let's make it so the game that doesn't assume it'll be played by a straight man&quot; even a political or controversial statement?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything that challenges the political and social hegemony of straight men in our current society in inherently political, because challenging the status quo is political.<br /> <br /> That it's controversial in 2019 is just a sad comment on how little progress we've made as a society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326651#post1326651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excuse me? Requiem and V5 did the exact opposite of that. They actually made the mechanics more in tune with the personal horror themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misunderstood me. We seem to be in agreement that Requiem and V5 moved to downplay the power fantasy/action aspects of the game and focus more on the horror side of the game.<br /> <br /> I was trying to say that those games put roadblocks to playing power fantasy straight out of the core books, not that they made the games about power fantasy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dont understand why the direct media adaptation of Vampire wouldn't try to be faithful to the source material, why they need to make it into a shallow power fantasy. </div> </div> </div>It's worth remembering that for all the cult classic status of Bloodlines 1, it's initial release was extremely poorly received, and killed Troika since the company simply did not have the resources to bring their intended game to fruition... and even trying bankrupted them. All the people that knew the Troika folks seem to disagree with your pessimism. Troika was an Icarus of a company that took on too big of a task, flew to high, and crashed for it, rather than a company out to play it safe.<br /> <br /> It's quite possible a better funded and staffed version of them could have done a better game with it... but it's long past a time to really know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Video games are the death of art. </div> </div> </div>No, they're not. Any more than all the other times people decried a new entertainment medium as the death of art (which is practically every time). Most entertainment based art is not high minded stuff, and it never has been, because entertaining has always beat out strong artistic vision. It's always been the rare talents that can meld vision and appeal, and create really special things. The problem is those are the ones we tend to remember and repeat as a culture; forgetting all the crap that was their competition at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T05:30:26-07:00","id":1326670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326652#post1326652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> snip<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/GRN1_EENfaE\" target=\"_blank\">How</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/SGGSXe3sK-g\" target=\"_blank\">About</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Ozd7G2mZT90\" target=\"_blank\">I just</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/5ECwhB21Pnk\" target=\"_blank\">Leave these</a><br /> <br /> Here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326644#post1326644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for Andromeda? A bugfest rushed during development with such great technical issues it became a meme. Andromeda didn't went down because it was &quot;woke&quot;, it went down because bioware has died of starvation and deadlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the reason why Andromeda failed, is because they abandoned it to work on Anthem, which is such an absolute shit fest, that Fallout 76 has more players still attending it right now.<br /> <br /> As for Andromeda itself, two of it's lead developers were an openly confirmed racist African American, who went onto social media and aggressively insulted white people. Even challenging them to physical conflicts for seemingly no reason whatsoever.<br /> <br /> As for the other, she was a hard core feminist, who seemed to take great pride in making the female models of the game as hideous and badly animated as possible, and then went on a rant towards the fans about how she didn't care if they thought the game looked ugly. Because making female models even slightly attractive set off her <i>&quot;that's objectifying women!&quot;</i> alarms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-22-2019, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T05:48:30-07:00","id":1326677,"title":"","content":"pls no arguing with videos, <br /> <br /> if those vids have any arguments/facts you'd like to use, <br /> better translate them in your post or link their sources (preferably not other vids)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T05:58:17-07:00","id":1326678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326677#post1326677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">pls no arguing with videos,<br /> <br /> if those vids have any arguments/facts you'd like to use,<br /> better translate them in your post or link their sources (preferably not other vids)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just seemed like the most expedient way to get the point across, since those people have already done the research and fact checking, not to mention are probably more educated / qualified to talk about the subject than I am.<br /> <br /> But alright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-22-2019, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T06:45:52-07:00","id":1326687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326654#post1326654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything that challenges the political and social hegemony of straight men in our current society in inherently political, because challenging the status quo is political.<br /> <br /> That it's controversial in 2019 is just a sad comment on how little progress we've made as a society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was more of a rhetorical question. Still, it seems that a discussion about Bloodlines has mostly turned into several people trying to argue with one person who is throwing around completely unsupported claims about entirely unrelated media and people who worked on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","user":"Morty","date":". 07-22-2019, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T07:27:37-07:00","id":1326692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1326678#post1326678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Just seemed like the most expedient way to get the point across, since those people have already done the research and fact, not to mention are probably more educated / qualified to talk about the subject than I am.<br /> <br /> But alright.</div> </div> </div> </div>just saying,<br /> <br /> heavy arms always makes the effort to properly present his arguments, with good english, and in a way that is very clear (even when the topic is complicated)<br /> <br /> I don't necessarily agree with him, but we owe it to him to at least make the same effort,<br /> and not using cheap tactics like videos (asking people to take time to watch them, and effectively adding 4 more people to the conversation, even though they're not even members in the forum),<br /> and not quoting his words as &quot;snip&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (not even sure what snip is supposed to mean lol)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Jo