sed to hold sexist ideas.<br /> <br /> We already had that with bloodlines 2 and choosing your pronouns - nice idea for any game but vampires. Unless you are playing as prince, so everyone has to kiss up to you, i dont see any kainite giving a rats ass about what YOU would like to be called. be glad if they dont call you by swears.<br /> <br /> and to this debate - sure some characters were highly sexualised like VV - so? Are you trying to tell me women that sexualise themselves voluntarely or use their physical attributes to their advantage dont exist? Its not always evil men forcing poor helpless women into wearing skimpy outfits. sometimes women dress slutty on purpose cause they know they will be able to play stupid men who mainly think with their genitals<br /> <br /> That said, i never once thought about sexism or male power fantasy in the game once. in special as you can play as female as well. My wife loves the game to this day and so does my daughter. I think we are turning away from egaliterianism cause we dont allow women agency and making descissions of their own. I saw different personalities in the game - like therese / jeanette. very different women. so were VV and ming xiao. because women re people too and some like Xand some like Y. i would have felt something missing if female characters werent diverse. Hek with Yuki you had a kickass female in there as well and she was mortal<br /> <br /> I guess the &quot;male power fantasy&quot; is aimed at VV stripping for you. I might add she does that after you being her pawn, always being ncie to ehr kissing up to her, like a good dog with his tongue out risking your unlife for her on multiple occasions. heck she sends you to kill a hunter for her! id call that a female power fantasy. shes playing the player character like a fiddle and all she has to do is make some naughty promises. and thats something i see the plyer falling for rather than the charater as vampires arent sexual creatures anymore.<br /> <br