age\">i think they were to preoccupied with finishing the game to polish it with things like multiple seduction targets</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, Bioware knew it was a lot of fun.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T16:31:32-07:00","id":1406348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406322#post1406322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that said why is this even a concern. Kainites share one sex and gender identity - fckn undead. anything else is of no concern anymore. they arent sexual or sexualised creatures. they are corpses</div> </div> </div> </div>When Mercurio tells the player character about Jeanette, he explains what he's told about how vampires aren't into sex, but Jeanette apparently is. The latter turns out to be true (or at least she does it). So she's an exception.<br /> Then when hunting the plague bearers, one of them is Jezebel, a woman spreading the disease to sex workers. I'm not sure I'd call what her desires sexual strictly speaking, but her term were decidedly carnal.<br /> Then there's VV. And even Ming Xiao says:<br /> &quot;The tongue lies limp and pasty if you're simply dead - otherwise you would do well to savor these little graces. Your eyes are still able to take in my form and the blood still rushes hot to your skin - must your organs die so selectively?&quot;<br /> <br /> So there we had four exceptions. Or maybe they were just affecting it to manipulate the player character. But if vampires don't want it, why bother to pretend? And why is only female kindred who express any sexuality, real or not? When this topic comes up, I'm often reminded of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p_XmrhUEIb0\" target=\"_blank\">a scene from <i>30 Rock</i></a>, adapted to depict the one ofthose four NPCs discussing how they're going to deal with the fledgling with one of the other five female kindred.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406327#post1406327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in what universe are progressive people anti-sex? It's certainly not this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some very young members of gay Twitter come close at least: don't wear leather harnesses at Pride, we should have special cafes where you don't go to hook up, 25 year olds shouldn't have sex with 20 year olds, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T18:29:40-07:00","id":1406364,"title":"","content":"Ugh... we're reviving this thread?<br /> <br /> Anyway:<br /> <br /> I'll say it again. The issue with Bloodlines isn't that it has sexy female vampires as characters. It's how they're used. It doesn't matter if women like the game too; lots of people like entertainment that has problems with some form of bigotry. Everyone is allowed to decide for themselves how they want to deal with bigotry (aimed at them or others) involved with the media they consume; we all do it because there's always some. It doesn't matter if a sexy female character is designed by a woman either; women aren't inherently anti-sexist. Lots of women actively promote sexism, and hordes more are still struggling with institutional and systemic sexism's subtle influence on their decision making.<br /> <br /> Ultimately what matters is execution.<br /> <br /> The Hannah/Jezebel part of the Plague quest-line is actually well executed from this regard. With minimal hitting the audience over the head with things, it highlights how Hannah's life was negatively impacted by the prudish and nasty way sex workers are treated by society, how easily a group of bad actors can abuse her because she has to live in the shadows, and how that abuse spreads to uninvolved people because of it. It's not about Hannah being evil because she's in the sex trade; the game rewards you for recognizing her humanity and feelings. It's about how society turns its back on &quot;undesirables&quot; both visible and invisible and abandons them to horrific dangers; and only really starts to care when people society cares about start to be negatively impacted.<br /> <br /> Jeannette is executed poorly. Her role in the story is to be a sex object for the player to either reject or accept. She exists to tell you that vampires can still have sex and annoy her sister. There's potential, as I said very early on, for something that could be a stronger statement and story, but what happens with Therese and Jeannette doesn't matter after you've handled them so you can get to Tung.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'll throw out something for anyone that wants to say they don't see anything surface level sexist in the game?<br /> <br /> Explain Poster Session, the side quest where you collect various random items, and give them to Gary, who rewards you with sexy posters for your Haven of female NPCs. There is literally no point to this fetch quest besides higher quality pictures of NPCs in little to no clothing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T20:44:56-07:00","id":1406373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406364#post1406364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh... we're reviving this thread?<br /> <br /> Anyway:<br /> <br /> I'll say it again. The issue with Bloodlines isn't that it has sexy female vampires as characters. It's how they're used. It doesn't matter if women like the game too; lots of people like entertainment that has problems with some form of bigotry. Everyone is allowed to decide for themselves how they want to deal with bigotry (aimed at them or others) involved with the media they consume; we all do it because there's always some. It doesn't matter if a sexy female character is designed by a woman either; women aren't inherently anti-sexist. Lots of women actively promote sexism, and hordes more are still struggling with institutional and systemic sexism's subtle influence on their decision making.<br /> <br /> Ultimately what matters is execution.<br /> <br /> The Hannah/Jezebel part of the Plague quest-line is actually well executed from this regard. With minimal hitting the audience over the head with things, it highlights how Hannah's life was negatively impacted by the prudish and nasty way sex workers are treated by society, how easily a group of bad actors can abuse her because she has to live in the shadows, and how that abuse spreads to uninvolved people because of it. It's not about Hannah being evil because she's in the sex trade; the game rewards you for recognizing her humanity and feelings. It's about how society turns its back on &quot;undesirables&quot; both visible and invisible and abandons them to horrific dangers; and only really starts to care when people society cares about start to be negatively impacted.<br /> <br /> Jeannette is executed poorly. Her role in the story is to be a sex object for the player to either reject or accept. She exists to tell you that vampires can still have sex and annoy her sister. There's potential, as I said very early on, for something that could be a stronger statement and story, but what happens with Therese and Jeannette doesn't matter after you've handled them so you can get to Tung.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'll throw out something for anyone that wants to say they don't see anything surface level sexist in the game?<br /> <br /> Explain Poster Session, the side quest where you collect various random items, and give them to Gary, who rewards you with sexy posters for your Haven of female NPCs. There is literally no point to this fetch quest besides higher quality pictures of NPCs in little to no clothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel honestly this is a very sex-negative attitude and as a sex-positive feminist, probably not a great one. There's nothing wrong with sex in entertainment as long as its consensual, fun, and empowering not degrading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T21:00:55-07:00","id":1406374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406373#post1406373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel honestly this is a very sex-negative attitude and as a sex-positive feminist, probably not a great one. There's nothing wrong with sex in entertainment as long as its consensual, fun, and empowering not degrading.</div> </div> </div> </div>But who gets to decide what is and is not degrading? And who gets the final word on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T22:32:10-07:00","id":1406382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406327#post1406327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in what universe are progressive people anti-sex? It's certainly not this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>IRL ^^ slut shaming and stuff, and surprisingly it wasnt the religious people who managed to get the women banned from formula 1, boxing and other entry modelling jobs cause thats &quot;objectifiyng&quot; women<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406348#post1406348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there we had four exceptions</div> </div> </div> </div>according to the rulebooks vampires dont have any such desires anymore, being corpses and such, however not having fun doing it doesnt mean they cant do it, as its also said that sometimes, sex is a reward given by kainites to their ghouls who crave it. Sex is more a tool in a kainites arsenal. that said ming xaio isnt kainite to begin with<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406364#post1406364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of women actively promote sexism</div> </div> </div> </div>im not going down the rabbid whole of what sexism is, because apparently sexism against men, even institutional is absolutly fine with such people. And its totally ignoring human psyche and biology because a lot of &quot;sexism&quot; is just human nature and has nothing to do with society at all, nor education or anything but hard wired neurology.<br /> Yes many women promote some form of sexism - because they like it. Same for men. So should we ban all fun and tell people what they have to like or be attracted to?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406364#post1406364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jeannette is executed poorly</div> </div> </div> </div>So you tell me you never met women like Jeanette? I did, and they usually are regulars in clubs and bars. My sister is one of those women. &quot;Girls just wanna have fun&quot; yes there are women who love to have sex and are easy to have because they are looking for people to have sex with a lot. I have a friend who became a hooker because she realised &quot;hey instead of spending money each weekend in clubs to get a guy, why not just let them pay me&quot; - and there she is a hooker who made her hobby into her profession.<br /> My sister still goes to clubs, in almost illegally sexy clothing, just having fun as she likes. so is she poorly executed?<br /> i thought of Jeanette as just one of &quot;those&quot; girls and cheered that the game has the balls to depict all kinds of women<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406364#post1406364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll throw out something for anyone that wants to say they don't see anything surface level sexist in the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>as i said in the other thread - EVERYTHING can be interpreted as sexist if you want to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406364#post1406364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Explain Poster Session</div> </div> </div> </div>with pleasure.<br /> You may not be aware but a lot of women like their bodies and make selfies of it in sexy or no clothing. quite some women even let photographers make sexy pics of them either for money or even hiring the photographer to do it. In special Pin Up art is rarely seen as porn and not that uncommon, i know quite some women you wouldnt expect having done this, like a female judge, or a carpenter, who have existing pin up art of themselves. My wife gifted me some pin up art of her to my birthday.<br /> So gary simply stole those and gave them to you in exchange for fetching stuff for him, and as nosferatu are all about ifnormation he likely knew you went into vesuvius and had your time with VV and Jeanette before, so his guess would be you might actually be into that form of payment and played accordingly. Maybe it was his way of telling you that he knows about you, knows your secrets and you better dont mess with the nosferatu. Maybe he had those posters anyway and that ex model nosferatu dsidnt want them around so he figured, giving them to you as payment kills 2 birds with 1 stone.<br /> <br /> For the player character those posters can also be more than just decoration. 1 they may help feel human and alive (humanity) they may also be used as potential blackmail items as im sure Damsel doesnt want that pinup showing up in the last round etc.<br /> <br /> that said....what is the fckn issue to begin with? Vampires is an adult game 18+. World of Darkness is a very very adult setting (the horror, graphic violence, the rulebooks art, the psychothriller and ofc the sex just look at the ghoul rulebooks they are straight up porn)<br /> <br /> if stuff like the vesuvius were missing, i would feel robbed of an aspect of WoD. Redemption also had its strip club. its just fitting a modern night setting cause what businesses are open in the middle of the night?<br /> <br /> Being austrian i am just surprised how many issues many americans see with stuff like this. Our government in corona just deemed brothels essential businesses XD<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406373#post1406373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing wrong with sex in entertainment as long as its consensual, fun, and empowering not degrading.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why cant it be degrading? You know there is a lot of people into that stuff, men and women? Just ask the BDSM community. We actually ahve scientific data and studies on that - about 10% of the total population are into some form of degrading and kinky stuff in the bedroom. Why cant we depict that? 10% of the population is about 4 times more than gay people and 100 times more than trans people and they get representation...<br /> <br /> Indeed given the theme of vampire and in special WoD: Ghoul i really had hoped for something in that direction. Why not have a little BDSM dungeon in your haven for Heather? Youd also get the lesbian checkmark if you play a female character^^<br /> Its not like including some kink will ban a game that already has strip clubs, sex, gore and horror<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406342#post1406342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, Bioware knew it was a lot of fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>and bioware went down the toilet in the last years as well. They lost their soul somewhere along the way and its a shame really, given they managed to make good and well written - and well received - lgbtq+ characters already in Baldurs gate, and made them great in Dragon Age origins and the Mass Effect trilogy. Ok Zevran was annoying but it also perfectly fitted his backstory so i didnt take offense at him being so extremely in yoru face with his sexuality, he ater all grew up as a brothel boy.<br /> <br /> I dont mind having well written characters of anything in a game, but lately it seems developers just want to cram lgbtq+ stuff into games and are so in your face about it it ruins the entire game and i feel offended by that blatant pandering. I dont want a gay person who happens to be a character in the game. i want a CHARACTER that happens to be gay in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 08-05-2020, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T00:51:34-07:00","id":1406396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406348#post1406348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And even Ming Xiao says:<br /> &quot;The tongue lies limp and pasty if you're simply dead - otherwise you would do well to savor these little graces. Your eyes are still able to take in my form and the blood still rushes hot to your skin - must your organs die so selectively?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ming is not a good example,<br /> kuei-jin do not suffer the same restrictions as cainites when it comes to sex,<br /> they can do it normally, enjoy it (a bit less than mortals) and can even reproduce<br /> <br /> also, when does she say that? I played the game many times and never had her say anything relating to sex<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So there we had four exceptions. </div> </div> </div>five. you forgot your sire at the start of the game<br /> <br /> and Mercurio is wrong, vampires can have sex, they just can't enjoy it without the kiss. EXCEPT for vampires with the Nymphomania/Satyriasis condition (Guide to the Sabbat, derangement section), which Jeanette or Jezebel may have","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 08-05-2020, 03:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T02:07:06-07:00","id":1406400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-mas