k":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T04:23:51-07:00","id":1406410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406342#post1406342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, Bioware knew it was a lot of fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>i don't see what that has to do with my statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T05:04:05-07:00","id":1406414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406396#post1406396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ming is not a good example,<br /> kuei-jin do not suffer the same restrictions as cainites when it comes to sex,<br /> they can do it normally, enjoy it (a bit less than mortals) and can even reproduce<br /> <br /> also, when does she say that? I played the game many times and never had her say anything relating to sex</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. It is only that line, if I'm even interpreting it correctly. It's part of the conversation with her outside the Hallowbrook Hotel. Although, it's a technicality that the beautiful, female secondary antagonist is a type of vampire that can enjoy sex.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406396#post1406396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">five. you forgot your sire at the start of the game</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right and that actually goes against my point, because if you play a woman, there is one male vampire who expresses sexuality. Although that's different from the other examples because the player character was alive at the time and could be expected to enjoy it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406396#post1406396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and Mercurio is wrong, vampires can have sex, they just can't enjoy it without the kiss. EXCEPT for vampires with the Nymphomania/Satyriasis condition (Guide to the Sabbat, derangement section), which Jeanette or Jezebel may have</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that all of them should like it or at that all them shouldn't like it, but those express or use sexuality, for itself or as a means to an end, in VTMB1, are either alive or female. Or the sire for the first 10 seconds or so of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T06:16:59-07:00","id":1406421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406364#post1406364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh... we're reviving this thread?<br /> <br /> Anyway:<br /> <br /> I'll say it again. The issue with Bloodlines isn't that it has sexy female vampires as characters. It's how they're used. It doesn't matter if women like the game too; lots of people like entertainment that has problems with some form of bigotry. Everyone is allowed to decide for themselves how they want to deal with bigotry (aimed at them or others) involved with the media they consume; we all do it because there's always some. It doesn't matter if a sexy female character is designed by a woman either; women aren't inherently anti-sexist. Lots of women actively promote sexism, and hordes more are still struggling with institutional and systemic sexism's subtle influence on their decision making.<br /> <br /> Ultimately what matters is execution.<br /> <br /> The Hannah/Jezebel part of the Plague quest-line is actually well executed from this regard. With minimal hitting the audience over the head with things, it highlights how Hannah's life was negatively impacted by the prudish and nasty way sex workers are treated by society, how easily a group of bad actors can abuse her because she has to live in the shadows, and how that abuse spreads to uninvolved people because of it. It's not about Hannah being evil because she's in the sex trade; the game rewards you for recognizing her humanity and feelings. It's about how society turns its back on &amp;quot;undesirables&amp;quot; both visible and invisible and abandons them to horrific dangers; and only really starts to care when people society cares about start to be negatively impacted.<br /> <br /> Jeannette is executed poorly. Her role in the story is to be a sex object for the player to either reject or accept. She exists to tell you that vampires can still have sex and annoy her sister. There's potential, as I said very early on, for something that could be a stronger statement and story, but what happens with Therese and Jeannette doesn't matter after you've handled them so you can get to Tung.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'll throw out something for anyone that wants to say they don't see anything surface level sexist in the game?<br /> <br /> Explain Poster Session, the side quest where you collect various random items, and give them to Gary, who rewards you with sexy posters for your Haven of female NPCs. There is literally no point to this fetch quest besides higher quality pictures of NPCs in little to no clothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>OMG seriously?<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t played Bloodlines so maybe I\u2019m like misinterpreting things but the poster thing sounds a lot like a guy giving another person nudes of girls they both know. Which as you know you are NOT supposed to do.<br /> <br /> I like being sexy too but something about the poster thing as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> described it just bothers me. But again I haven\u2019t played the game so maybe I\u2019m taking it out of context, plus if that\u2019s the only sexist thing about it I mean it\u2019s not horrible or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T06:17:55-07:00","id":1406422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406410#post1406410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i don't see what that has to do with my statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying there's a huge fanbase for romances in-universe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406374#post1406374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But who gets to decide what is and is not degrading? And who gets the final word on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, it's a combination of the artist and the audience. The artist is the person who decides what they view as acceptable and the audience is the one who judges with their wallets. People aren't the same obviously and have different levels of tolerance or desire from their media.<br /> <br /> Liana Kerzner is a favorite Youtube personality of mine and she's a person who reviews video games as a woman and feminist. One of her most angry long rants was about the costume changes to Mortal Kombat's female characters because she feels like they're being singled out because of a desire to appear progressive while ignoring that women like the cartoonish overthetop stuff as much as the men.<br /> <br /> &quot;And if it's women being told what's sexist and what's not, how has anything improved?&quot;<br /> <br /> Sex is a big part of Vampire: The Masqerade and the big thing should be making it appeal to both male and female audiences. Which to me says the only difference for Bloodlines was they should have put in more men for women to seduce and maybe a few models for them as well. The absence of such is partially why La Croix of all people has the biggest female following of its male characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-05-2020, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T06:38:21-07:00","id":1406426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406422#post1406422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Saying there's a huge fanbase for romances in-universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate the way Bioware handles romance","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T06:43:04-07:00","id":1406427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406421#post1406421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven\u2019t played Bloodlines so maybe I\u2019m like misinterpreting things but the poster thing sounds a lot like a guy giving another person nudes of girls they both know. Which as you know you are NOT supposed to do.<br /> I hate the way Bioware handles romance</div> </div> </div> </div>Dont worry its pin up art not actual nudes, and the girls definitely posed for them. We dont know how gary obtained them, could be they actuall posed for him or maybe for someone else and he stole it. That said, vampires are constantly killing people, violating the law each night, and with all the blood and gore stealing some girls pics and share them really isnt something that would bother me. more like the trace of dead people you leave behind.<br /> I mean you are basicly violating the blood dolls, kinda raping them, im a bit amused you find sharing pics the issue XD<br /> <br /> to romance - i liked the morrigan one in Dragon Age 1 or viconia in baldurs gate. and man i loved Tali in Mass effect 2&amp;3 a bit cheesy maybe but i liked it.<br /> the only male romance options i played were alistair and Garrus. I liked the later and alistair...was always weird in the head<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406422#post1406422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Liana Kerzner is a favorite Youtube personality of mine and she's a person who reviews video games as a woman and feminist. One of her most angry long rants was about the costume changes to Mortal Kombat's female characters because she feels like they're being singled out because of a desire to appear progressive while ignoring that women like the cartoonish overthetop stuff as much as the men.</div> </div> </div> </div>Afaik she also noted that female fighters DO fight in very short outfits. cause clothing gets in the way. Me as martial artist im totally liking the bodysuit outfits - a bikini might be ok for a woman with small breasts but any normal or big requires serious bras. That said men also just fight in shorts because...<br /> <br /> - clothing can be grabbed and used against you<br /> - clothing contributes to overheating your body, which is bad for many reasons<br /> - clothing limits the ways you can move<br /> - for females, fighting in sexy clothing against a male opponent is actually a real life working advantage as guys will be more resistant to hit, hit lighter and may be staring at boobs instead of blocking amn incoming punch.<br /> <br /> so yes bare handed fighters want to strip down as much aspossible - both sexes. unless the clothing is acutal armor then you want as much of it as possible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T06:55:14-07:00","id":1406429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406422#post1406422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Saying there's a huge fanbase for romances in-universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>as nice as that is it is completely unrelated to my point. which was that a more fleshed out romancing would be lower on the priority list of things they couldn't finish. like chinatown","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T07:16:29-07:00","id":1406431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406422#post1406422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Saying there's a huge fanbase for romances in-universe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ultimately, it's a combination of the artist and the audience. The artist is the person who decides what they view as acceptable and the audience is the one who judges with their wallets. People aren't the same obviously and have different levels of tolerance or desire from their media.<br /> <br /> Liana Kerzner is a favorite Youtube personality of mine and she's a person who reviews video games as a woman and feminist. One of her most angry long rants was about the costume changes to Mortal Kombat's female characters because she feels like they're being singled out because of a desire to appear progressive while ignoring that women like the cartoonish overthetop stuff as much as the men.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;And if it's women being told what's sexist and what's not, how has anything improved?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Sex is a big part of Vampire: The Masqerade and the big thing should be making it appeal to both male and female audiences. Which to me says the only difference for Bloodlines was they should have put in more men for women to seduce and maybe a few models for them as well. The absence of such is partially why La Croix of all people has the biggest female following of its male characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely agree with the last paragraph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T07:23:00-07:00","id":1406433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406373#post1406373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel honestly this is a very sex-negative attitude and as a sex-positive feminist, probably not a great one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel quiet honestly this is a reflexive defensive response that doesn't critically think in the slightest about what I said. I have my issues with how the game uses VV, but at least it lets you make a reasonable case she does what she does because she actually likes it. It's far too easy to make the case that Jeannette doesn't actually care about sex for the sake of pleasure, but rather as an emotional tool against her sister, and for dealing with her deep seated traumatic issues from childhood.<br /> <br /> Being a sex-positive feminist doesn't mean every artistic or entertainment based depiction of women having sex has to be defended. Sex-positive feminism is well past its bickering with anti-porn activists as the majority in both camps got on board with going after the patriarchal control over sex-based industries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's nothing wrong with sex in entertainment as long as its consensual, fun, and empowering not degrading. </div> </div> </div>And my point is that Jeannette isn't actually an empowering figure, and there is a whole side quest that's degrading on its face; and it's not exactly alone. I don't think this thread has touched on the fact that you can get XP for helping to slut-shame and cyberbully a woman so badly she commits suicide and you only get dinged Humanity if you take the money for the job; is that a sex-positive message?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406382#post1406382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the women banned from formula 1, boxing and other entry modelling jobs cause thats &quot;objectifiyng&quot; women...</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear, you're talking about F1 and boxing getting rid of grid girls and ring girls? Women who's only actual function is to stand there and look pretty during lulls in their sports?<br /> <br /> Since F1 has no rules against mixed gender racing, and boxing still has segregated divisions but has women's divisions as well as men's ones, it seems important to be clear.<br /> <br /> I don't know about you, but I'd rather see F1's attention on promoting women in the cars (since you rarely see much major covered of anything but the Grand Prix, a lot of women in F1 get zero recognition outside of dedicated fans that actually watch the lower divisions) than women smiling for cameras... F1's not a model promoting organization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> im not going down the rabbid whole of what sexism is, because apparently sexism against men, even institutional is absolutly fine with such people. </div> </div> </div>This is one heck of a non-sequitur. You're comfortable enough with a definition of sexism that you say you don't see any in Bloodlines, but you're not willing to discuss it because... there are women that promote sexist views out there?<br /> <br /> What does sexism against men have to do with any of it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And its totally ignoring human psyche and biology because a lot of &quot;sexism&quot; is just human nature and has nothing to do with society at all, nor education or anything but hard wired neurology. </div> </div> </div>Citation needed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes many women promote some form of sexism - because they like it. Same for men. So should we ban all fun and tell people what they have to like or be attracted to? </div> </div> </div>Are you claiming rape should be legal because the rapist enjoys it? How about child molestation?<br /> <br /> If we've gotten past the hyperbolic pearl clutching part of this and recognized that what is and isn't appropriate to tolerate as a society is something that exists on a scale, not a binary of either pro- or anti-sex, lets get back the point of the thread: is there sexism in Bloodlines 1? Not &quot;should it be censored, banned, or removed from circulation,&quot; just, does it have sexist elements in it?<br /> <br /> Because how to respond to what's present relies on acknowledging what's there. I think Bloodlines 1 has sexist elements in it, but I still play it, and I'd still recommend it because I think most people can enjoy despite that. I might warn people about there being some squicky side quests and that the game certainly doesn't shy from sex being present in good and bad ways, but WW screwing up their intended message is something WW fans of all generations generally have come to terms with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you tell me you never met women like Jeanette? </div> </div> </div>Nobody has, because vampires aren't real and MPD/DID doesn't work like that (and I have a friend that's into blood play kink, is diagnosed with DID, and most of their female identities are very sexually active... so I can say from experience that pretty much the closest combination you'll find IRL is still nothing like the game character). Thankfully women, like all humans, can't be distilled down to a single thing like how much they enjoy sex, and whether or not a woman is like Jeanette is not, in most people's minds, strictly going to be whether she likes sex or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> so is she poorly executed? </div> </div> </div>She's not a character in a fictional story subject to literary critical analysis. Jeannette is a character in a story, what the creators of that story do with her matters to the qualities one can attach to that work in a way that doesn't translate to real world people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> i thought of Jeanette as just one of &quot;those&quot; girls and cheered that the game has the balls to depict all kinds of women </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between tokenism and actual representation/diversity. Sex-positive women in Bloodlines 1 are far more frequently tokens than representatives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> as i said in the other thread - EVERYTHING can be interpreted as sexist if you want to. </div> </div> </div>I do not want, but that doesn't mean I don't have lines about what is and isn't sexist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You may not be aware but a lot of women like their bodies and make selfies of it in sexy or no clothing. </div> </div> </div>Are you aware we're talking about a game that was released three years before the first iPhone came out and long before modern selfie culture?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So gary simply stole those and gave them to you in exchange for fetching stuff for him, and as nosferatu are all about ifnormation he likely knew you went into vesuvius and had your time with VV and Jeanette before, so his guess would be you might actually be into that form of payment and played accordingly. </div> </div> </div>I'm not asking why Gary might have been able to do it, I'm asking you to explain why it's even in the game other than to degrade women by focusing on them as sex objects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe it was his way of telling you that he knows about you, knows your secrets and you better dont mess with the nosferatu. </div> </div> </div>He does that about a dozen times directly to your face in the main quest line. It's a completely optional side quest. Gary does nothing to do you if you don't do it... even to that Masquerade breaching photograph of a Nosferatu you have that you give up as part of the quest. If the game wanted to make this happen, it could have and didn't. Imalia has a quest you do to get on her good side after pissing her off, so if the goal was to have Gary illustrate what the Nosferatu can do if you piss him off... Poster Session could have been the result of dialog options where you take a piss on the Nosferatu (esp. ones they he wasn't supposed to be there for!).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1 they may help feel human and alive (humanity) they may also be used as potential blackmail items as im sure Damsel doesnt want that pinup showing up in the last round etc. </div> </div> </div>Neither of these options are part of the game. If you want to regain Humanity for feeling human, you can do that (once) by dancing at one of the clubs. There is no similar hidden way to gain Humanity from this side quest. And given those posters (at least in the standard version) are all of vampires, it's not really a logical connection with Humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> that said....what is the fckn issue to begin with? </div> </div> </div>With Poster Session? The game awards you for doing a quest that's only actualized goal in the game is to decorate your haven with sexy posters of major female NPCs. The message of the game with that isn't sex-positive, just sexist.<br /> <br /> It's not there for setting or atmosphere (it looks really dumb in some of the Havens), you have no say in whether to hang the posters or not, it doesn't actually highlight any important message from the game. There's no ding against your Humanity for violating women's privacy (VV will get you a picture of her if you want one, you don't need Gary) to emphasize what a predator you're acting like. It's there to be eye candy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if stuff like the vesuvius were missing, i would feel robbed of an aspect of WoD. Redemption also had its strip club. its just fitting a modern night setting cause what businesses are open in the middle of the night? </div> </div> </div>Nobody said there shouldn't be a strip club in the game. This conversation would probably go better with actually talking about what people are saying, not railing against vague American Puritanical crap (which should be railed against, but complaining about it doesn't main everything else is OK).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being austrian i am just surprised how many issues many americans see with stuff like this. </div> </div> </div>Our country is full of Puritanical assholes and any hope at a discussion about a lot of these topics requires an actual appreciation of nuance and ability to navigate that everything has problems in it, and sometimes the assholes are right about it, but the only way to keep them from banning everything is to be able to say, &quot;OK that is bad, but all this stuff over here is good.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Our government in corona just deemed brothels essential businesses </div> </div> </div>Um.. citation needed? As far as I can tell Austria just reopened brothels as part of a general relaxation of shutdown rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why cant it be degrading? </div> </div> </div>Degrading, in this context, is not humiliation as part of a consensual form of adult play acting, but the active promotion of derogatory attitudes towards a group.<br /> <br /> That is, the difference between a woman that wants to be called a socially taboo word in private with a consenting partner, versus publicly using that word to describe all women.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dont mind having well written characters of anything in a game, but lately it seems developers just want to cram lgbtq+ stuff into games and are so in your face about it it ruins the entire game and i feel offended by that blatant pandering. </div> </div> </div>And a lot of us feel that too many of the characters in Bloodlines 1 are just pandering... so you do seem to get the idea here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T07:27:18-07:00","id":1406436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406426#post1406426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hate the way Bioware handles romance</div> </div> </div> </div>Serious question: How w