ssic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406796#post1406796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> MD also suffered from the immense amount of &quot;Video Game Developers being greedy bastards&quot; that would almost kill Battlefront II.<br /> <br /> * Unwanted Multiplayer Mode<br /> * Pay to Win Microtransactions<br /> * Removing <b>an hour </b>of gameplay to make a DLC they could sell (Where you catch the bomber who blew up the train station)<br /> * Never actually giving the villain any backstory or reason to do what he did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya everything with the DLC in the prequel games has been a letdown, disjointed from the rest of the story, even the missing link stuff for HR. I don't know anybody who was interested in that silly hacking game they spent all that time on for MD and it barely featured in the single player game. The story just didn't go anywhere in MD, either. Combat and abilities were a bit more well executed than HR, but that's about the only thing it has over HR.<br /> <br /> I do actually dig that it went from augs being available to help everyone (at least that could afford it) to being restricted to only the rich, powerful and influential to work their way to the setting of the original Deus Ex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T10:54:24-07:00","id":1406813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406810#post1406810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - Star Wars original trilogy Vader/Sidious and the empire<br /> - 1st edition Sabbat</div> </div> </div> </div>Sticking with the 1st Edition Sabbat, I have an appreciation for the fact they're mysterious and intimidating rather than warmed-over inferior Anarchs. With the Sabbat of 1st Edition, their ultimate goals and occult purposes can be filled in by the Storyteller and you can impose upon them any number of possible motivations or dangers.<br /> <br /> The Satanic element is also one that I actually approve of because the idea of a game that incorporates so much idea of literal Biblical evil and power means that you should have some people who are 100% on the side of the Devil and unapologetically so. Certainly, if you're Damned by your Embrace then there's a question, &quot;Why worry about selling your soul? Go all in.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2nd Edition Sabbat talk about freedom and a variety of religious beliefs while denying they're evil. Which means they're cowards and pathetic fools who are just a bunch of teenage Edgelords versus something that EMBRACES the inner darkness. The Infernalists are the &quot;real&quot; Sabbat and the highest ranking Cardinal is not fit to lick the boots of the lowest ranking Infernalist.<br /> <br /> Revised corrected a lot of these flaws as they weren't afraid to have the REAL Sabbat return who embrace their inner horrors.<br /> <br /> Bwhahahaha.<br /> <br /> :I leave it to you to determine how serious I am above:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T11:20:27-07:00","id":1406816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-i