ps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T12:33:22-07:00","id":1406825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406817#post1406817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One should lead to the others.<br /> <br /> My issue with the 2nd Edition was the fact that they dipped into the Anarch's thing too much. It also contradicted the fact they were a rigidly controlled theistic military.<br /> <br /> Two things that don't shout FREEDOM!</div> </div> </div> </div>what's your opinion on the sabbat from the 1st ed book <i>Blood Bond</i> ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T13:00:40-07:00","id":1406826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406825#post1406825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> what's your opinion on the sabbat from the 1st ed book <i>Blood Bond</i> ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I felt like that particular book had a lot of underdevelopment as it attempted to frame the villain of the story as a kind of Byronic hero taking much-deserved revenge on his former tormentor. I don't really think that most Sabbat packs would approve of going to such elaborate lengths for a Kine ghoul, though. The Sabbat are fine with revenge, that's a perfectly valid motive for a pack to support one of their members, but finding out it's all about an ordinary human girl from your Kine days?<br /> <br /> I feel like the Sabbat should have either killed or Embraced her.<br /> <br /> In fact, I think that would make the story much more interesting to have them turn on their &quot;friend&quot; mid-story.<br /> <br /> Is it more monstrous that way? Perhaps overtly so? Yes, but more interesting I feel.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T13:03:22-07:00","id":1406827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406813#post1406813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sticking with the 1st Edition Sabbat, I have an appreciation for the fact they're mysterious and intimidating rather than warmed-over inferior Anarchs. With the Sabbat of 1st Edition, their ultimate goals and occult purposes can be filled in by the Storyteller and you can impose upon them any number of possible motivations or dangers.<br /> <br /> The Satanic element is also one that I actually approve of because the idea of a game that incorporates so much idea of literal Biblical evil and power means that you should have some people who are 100% on the side of the Devil and unapologetically so. Certainly, if you're Damned by your Embrace then there's a question, &amp;quot;Why worry about selling your soul? Go all in.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> 2nd Edition Sabbat talk about freedom and a variety of religious beliefs while denying they're evil. Which means they're cowards and pathetic fools who are just a bunch of teenage Edgelords versus something that EMBRACES the inner darkness. The Infernalists are the &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; Sabbat and the highest ranking Cardinal is not fit to lick the boots of the lowest ranking Infernalist.<br /> <br /> Revised corrected a lot of these flaws as they weren't afraid to have the REAL Sabbat return who embrace their inner horrors.<br /> <br /> Bwhahahaha.<br /> <br /> :I leave it to you to determine how serious I am above:</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you\u2019re mostly kidding \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T00:54:06-07:00","id":1406916,"title":"","content":"To romances in gaming - it is a game after all. Cause if you want a realistic romance it should be 2 sided not one sided and your romance options should also put in effort to win your affection. Its very rare ive seen that happen in games.<br /> As for BG2 - viconias romance is not only tough but i really have to question myself why i would even try to persue her. shes not exactly the type of person you want to have around, lest be in a relation with, she is extremely tough to crack and all you get from it is being her pet for sex and an imaginery achievement.<br /> And Aerie is just a child in an adults body. Jaheira is so independant she wont even enter a real relationship with you no matter how good you handle her romance. its friends with benefits.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile in Mass Effect i had the feeling that the party im pursuing is also trying to win me over. Take Talis romance. she is willing to endanger her life so you can have sex with her, she is willing to leave her people for you, she does try to surprise you with nice things. On the other hand she is also demanding, she wont fly with all your BS, she wants you to do certain things for or with her. I found that to be rather realistic. Now you can argue how realistic (given her people were close to banning her anyway or actually did depending on your choices)<br /> Finding out she was seeing the doc to surprise me with something was a really nice change of the usual. See say dragon age - all you do is kiss up to your romance option so they like you (yes you can do it with presents but thats almost cheating) and they put in zero effort on their side. if i was on the more....progressive side id say that is teaching the player abusive behaviour is totally ok and the norm. But i think...its a game...<br /> <br /> id like to comment on heavy arms but i dont want to be the reason he gets banned for coming back to this so ill leave that<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406564#post1406564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That some people like it is irrelevant when the game media is causing harm.</div> </div> </div> </div>this is psychologicly speaking just BS. We dont apply that same standard to books or movies or any other area of entertainment. Watching a violent movie doesnt make you a violent person. watching a boxing match doesnt make you beat up people in the streets, visiting a strip club doesnt turn you into a mysoginist but somehow if a game depicts something its a problem? I play shooters a lot. IRL i never shot anyone, i dont even own a gun and i dont even want to. I played WoW for a long time and managed to not kill someone with an axe. Heck i play vampires and still dont drink blood. amazing innit?<br /> There arent any viable studies showing a correlation between games played and actual behaviour of people. The only exception being that during playing gamers are more aggressive, but less agressive after playing. same is true for martial arts too btw.<br /> <br /> That said WoD is based on the real world. It doesnt get the usual excuse of making fantasy better than real life cause its fantasy. WoD is the wrong franchise for this. There is fantasy worlds that are without sexism, racism, or any ism. WoD is based on a world where all those things are sadly a part of reality - and thats why i think they not only can but should be depicted.<br /> And you dont have to do it in a promotive way - how about the racist is later taken down by some black kainites BECAUSE he was racist towards them?<br /> As for VV and sexism - shes clearly the one in charge here and using her assets to play with her toys. i mean the men in her club. And the repercussion for her behaviour is that she will be seen as a slut by many. how is that an issue? (that said i dont think theres anything wrong with being a slut either, let people be people)<br /> Like how about some sexist pig mistreating VV for her being a slut? And then imagine how VV will get back at them to take revenge. You can entirely show that such behaviours have consequences. lethal ones even.<br /> indeed i would think VV would like her opponents to see her as depraved slut. Cause that makes them underestimate her and she will only have an easier time taking them out cause they will be blind to her abilities and powers<br /> <br /> And i see that in players too. apparently Therese is totally cool and fine but Jeanette is just a mans wet dream and sexist? Fact aside they are the same person, i can see non malkavians playing this game for the benefits of being underestimated on purpose. Jeanette is, even in her miniskirt, a powerfull influential rich kainite and no matter her behaviour doesnt change who and what she is. Can we stop acting as if someones choice of clothing is their entire personality?<br /> <br /> That said WoD is a franchise that is for adults only, for good reason. Not only of the horror and gore and psychothriller elements and all the evil of the DARK side of the world, it also published books like the ghul rulebooks - just look at the cover art and tell me sex and depracity arent a core element of the franchise.<br /> And i dont want it to be watered down bnecause people feel offended - play a different franchise then. There is a LOT of options out there for you. For people who like this dark world, there are only very very few options avalaiable.<br /> <br /> I rememebr ahving that discussion on a conan exiles RP server. if you cant handle the fact that slavery and indeed sex slavery is a part of that game....play a different one. Id argue the entire hyborean setting isnt somthing for you but there is also conan based games like age of conan where they toned down those aspects a lot. they are still in the game but more subtle and not all around, that said its called conan EXILES for a reason and in a lawless prison colony where they throw in murderers and rapists...whad did you expect exactly<br /> <br /> and since this will be giving the wrong vibes again (at this point ill draw my - i am actually autistic - card so some shit i say may come of the wrong way) ill want tos ay that i also play child friendly rpgs with my family and i enjoy those as well.<br /> Its almost like i like different franchises for different reasons just like i dont want to eat burgers all day and occasionally like some chinese food. but the moment my chinese restaurant starts banning chinese food caue of cultural appropriation stuff and only sells burgers, im mad. Let WoD be distinct from other franchises. please","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 08-08-2020, 04:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T02:07:14-07:00","id":1406923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406916#post1406916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">watching a boxing match doesnt make you beat up people in the streets</div> </div> </div> </div>actually, assault numbers are b