od reason. Not only of the horror and gore and psychothriller elements and all the evil of the DARK side of the world, it also published books like the ghul rulebooks - just look at the cover art and tell me sex and depracity arent a core element of the franchise.<br /> And i dont want it to be watered down bnecause people feel offended - play a different franchise then. There is a LOT of options out there for you. For people who like this dark world, there are only very very few options avalaiable.<br /> <br /> I rememebr ahving that discussion on a conan exiles RP server. if you cant handle the fact that slavery and indeed sex slavery is a part of that game....play a different one. Id argue the entire hyborean setting isnt somthing for you but there is also conan based games like age of conan where they toned down those aspects a lot. they are still in the game but more subtle and not all around, that said its called conan EXILES for a reason and in a lawless prison colony where they throw in murderers and rapists...whad did you expect exactly<br /> <br /> and since this will be giving the wrong vibes again (at this point ill draw my - i am actually autistic - card so some shit i say may come of the wrong way) ill want tos ay that i also play child friendly rpgs with my family and i enjoy those as well.<br /> Its almost like i like different franchises for different reasons just like i dont want to eat burgers all day and occasionally like some chinese food. but the moment my chinese restaurant starts banning chinese food caue of cultural appropriation stuff and only sells burgers, im mad. Let WoD be distinct from other franchises. please</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess romances can be handled more realistically in tabletop RPGs or MMOs with other players than in regular video games like Bloodlines. Trying to simulate romance (or even sex) by interacting with an AI is always inherently limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T06:02:52-07:00","id":1406955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406953#post1406953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess romances can be handled more realistically in tabletop RPGs or MMOs with other players than in regular video games like Bloodlines. Trying to simulate romance (or even sex) by interacting with an AI is always inherently limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>for sure but i think it has also to do with personal preferences and taste. Humans have different thoughts about what is romantic and what isnt, what an dieal relationship should look like, what they want from a partner etc. and some people have quite weird views on all of these but hey if it makes you happy.<br /> and while you cant represent all of those i guess if you make gay relationships a thing despite it affecting a small minority, why not then include other minorities as well and their relationships.<br /> <br /> Id for once really like to see something different. But i also realise thats dditional work that will not have big impacts on sales so well. Then again i think it would fit perfectly into WoD rather than other franchises. (though not really in vampire as i dont see vampies really wanting relationships of love on a bigger scale that would be a rare exception in my book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 08-08-2020, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T07:21:32-07:00","id":1406960,"title":"","content":"Sadly, I haven't heard any hint that there will be romances in Bloodlines 2. Mind you, the only long-lasting relationship you can cultivate in Bloodlines 1 that goes anywhere is with Heather...and she's your slave.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That &quot;romance&quot; was one that was designed also to make players uncomfortable and encourage those with High Humanity to free her as all she was feeling was artificial--no matter how useful she was. It was an &quot;anti-romance&quot; and a very effective one at that.<br /> <br /> Keiron Gillen (Doctor Aphra, Young Avengers) discusses it here: <a href=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/2008/04/09/vampire-bloodlines-heather-and-me/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/200...eather-and-me/</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cPower Corrupts\u201d has never been true. In my experience, Power Seduces. \u201cCorrupt\u201d implies it\u2019s akin to sprinkling a little shit in an otherwise immaculate meal. The problem with power is that it just makes everything better. And when someone\u2019s staring up at you, saying you\u2019re the best person in the world and they\u2019d do anything \u2013 <i>anything</i> \u2013 you ask, could you say no?<br /> <br /> I thought I could. I was wrong.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been on adventures before, and I always lean towards the side of right. I tried to do that here too but since entering the World of Darkness, even best intentions twisted in my hand. Heather was the classic case. I found her, lying dying in the corner of a Santa Monica emergency ward. A college girl with market-bought Scarlet dyed hair and emo glasses, straight off an Oakland campus. Pity makes me choose to feed her a drop of my own Vampiric blood, gifting her a little of my own power \u2013 enough to save her. She becomes what we call a Ghoul. Coming to, she asks me what happened. In a moment of madness, I tell her the truth. She screams, calling for the police and I make with the disappearing into the night thing my brethren and I do so well.<br /> <br /> I forget about her. So when, much later, she turns up outside the LA Camarilla\u2019s headquarters it\u2019s a surprise. She\u2019d been looking for me everywhere since that night. She hasn\u2019t been able to stop thinking about me. She just wants to be there for me, pay me back any way she can, whatever. I try and talk her out of it \u2013 she really doesn\u2019t know what she\u2019s getting into, but she\u2019s so insistent. I think \u201cwhy not\u201d. I\u2019ll treat her well and everything will be okay.<br /> <br /> I take her back to my sanctuary and tell her what\u2019s going on. She doesn\u2019t believe me at first. \u201cVampire and Ghoul?\u201d she asks, \u201cIs that some kind of Fetish<br /> Slang?\u201d. I persist and the stain of truth sinks into her. But when she recovers from the initial horror, she doesn\u2019t care. She loves me in the way the flame loves the air or the arm loves the needle, except a thousand times worse. I know it\u2019s fake and it\u2019s only what I did to her that made her like this. But no matter how artificial the affection is, it\u2019s still a tongue lapping my ego.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/images/april08/heather2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> She gives me a little of her money and offers up her neck for me to drink from. I try and treat her as politely as I can, but she\u2019s so damn submissive, I find myself falling into the role of master. I\u2019ve got a beautiful girl who\u2019ll do anything I ask her too, quickly, obediently. Since she wants to serve so badly, I find myself giving her tasks and demands that I\u2019d never make to anyone else. And, to my horror, I like it. I have to leave heading out for serious business, but I surprise even myself with my final command: Change your appearance. She went to the bathroom, a happy slave and I head out into the eternal night.<br /> \u201cIs that some Fetish slang?\u201d. Heh. It may as well have been.<br /> <br /> My work takes me into a hellish place, full of violence and madness, but it\u2019s my internal turmoil that\u2019s confusing me. This isn\u2019t like me at all, but the opportunity was there and what was the real harm? She thinks she loves me. It makes her happy. And in a sordid kind of way, it makes me happy too. As I progress around the dilapidated mansion full of knives and the men who wield them, I start thinking that the insanity of the place as some kind of reflection of my inner turmoil\u2026 but then realise that\u2019s yet more egotism. How did I find myself in this place? I think back to the chain terribly slutty, manipulative things I\u2019ve done since being embraced, and I wonder if you\u2019ve been falling long enough, you even notice anymore.<br /> <br /> I deliberately put off returning home until I close all business, but the nagging questions haunts me. What\u2019s going to happen when I walk through the door? How will she look? How will I feel? <i>Will I like it?</i> I step inside.<br /> <br /> Heather\u2019s changed. Bits of red hair show in scarlet slashes through the fresh black. Green eyes drowning in kohl, hair a halo and body wrapped in something tight, black and shiny. Her idea of what a Vampire\u2019s servant should look like. She\u2019s not far wrong.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/images/april08/heather3.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> She\u2019s made the effort so, it seems, should I. I let her suckle some more of my blood from an opened wrist, cementing our relationship a drop at a time. I\u2019ve been told that three feedings lead to a bond of an intensity unknown in all other life, and this is one more step towards that. At that second, I don\u2019t really care. She\u2019s my ghoul. I\u2019m her Vampire. She lives for me and I take what I desire. It\u2019s the natural order, for my kind, and I\u2019m almost exulting in it.<br /> <br /> At which point, she throws down a pile of greasy notes in my lap. Her college fund, she announces, and she wants me to have it. After all, she doesn\u2019t need it anymore. She\u2019s going to drop out of school so she could look after me properly, like she knows she really should. It\u2019s like a slap to the face. I wake up.<br /> <br /> Sure, I was a vampire, but there was no need to be one I was slouching towards. I told her she had to go. She screamed denial. I insisted, saying that this was to be my last order to her. Distraught, she\u2019s begs for another chance. And even there, there was some part of me that was thinking \u201cGo on: You deserve to be worshiped, and you can spend the money on especially Bloody Marys and shotgun rounds\u201d. But I gritted my teeth, rammed a stake through that part of my heart and hoped it stayed lodged there long enough to do what I had to do. Eventually, she left. I breathed a sigh. Or regret or relief, I really couldn\u2019t tell.<br /> <br /> I may be a Vampire. I don\u2019t have to suck. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-08-2020, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T07:47:01-07:00","id":1406967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406960#post1406960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, I haven't heard any hint that there will be romances in Bloodlines 2. Mind you, the only long-lasting relationship you can cultivate in Bloodlines 1 that goes anywhere is with Heather...and she's your slave.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That &amp;quot;romance&amp;quot; was one that was designed also to make players uncomfortable and encourage those with High Humanity to free her as all she was feeling was artificial--no matter how useful she was. It was an &amp;quot;anti-romance&amp;quot; and a very effective one at that.<br /> <br /> Keiron Gillen (Doctor Aphra, Young Avengers) discusses it here: <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/2008/04/09/vampire-bloodlines-heather-and-me/&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/200...eather-and-me/</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like romance better than anti-romance but I guess both have their place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T07:58:41-07:00","id":1406969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406967#post1406967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like romance better than anti-romance but I guess both have their place.</div> </div> </div> </div>The big issue with Bloodlines is every character disappears after you leave a space except Nines, La Croix, and Ming Xiao. Which of course hurts any character development.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T08:16:26-07:00","id":1406974,"title":"","content":"So I don't think it was sexist as in &quot;men are better&quot;, but it sure as heck was targeted to my demographic at that time (young straight male). As a now older straight male, I hope the new one takes a more Dragon Age approach with it. There were characters for most every orientation to flirt with and thirst over, and some of them were closed off to you depending on your character (just like real life!). I love what I have seen in the previews and will absolutely be getting this day one. If romance and sex are going to be included, let everyone have some fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T10:14:24-07:00","id":1406990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406960#post1406960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, I haven't heard any hint that there will be romances in Bloodlines 2. Mind you, the only long-lasting relationship you can cultivate in Bloodlines 1 that goes anywhere is with Heather...and she's your slave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I fostered great lasting relationships in that game; Mercutio is my man, Fat Larry is my brother, and the woman with the big tits in the cathedral gives me money. What's more romantic than a good partnership? <br /> <br /> <br /> Serious note: <br /> <br /> The Ideal for romance in a VTM game would be no more, no less, than finding people at clubs or bars and sweet talking your way into getting a drink. That's the romance vampires need. The goal isn't to fuck pretty people, it's to drink from them, or to have them serve you, and I think that's something worth emphasizing. Offer me a bar, offer me a gay bar, offer me a BDSM club. The person's personality doesn't matter, we're not in a place with music this loud to have a good talk; we want blood. Feed on site or take them home, it doesn't matter, the blood matters. A beautifully written, well crafted romantic narrative is going to take resources and isn't going to hit all players, but this? This is simple, and players understand what it means to the character more than they do a sappy romance that doesn't click for them. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T14:25:11-07:00","id":1407029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1406990#post1406990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, I fostered great lasting relationships in that game; Mercutio is my man, Fat Larry is my brother, and the woman with the big tits in the cathedral gives me money. What's more romantic than a good partnership? <br /> <br /> <br /> Serious note: <br /> <br /> The Ideal for romance in a VTM game would be no more, no less, than finding people at clubs or bars and sweet talking your way into getting a drink. That's the romance vampires need. The goal isn't to fuck pretty people, it's to drink from them, or to have them serve you, and I think that's something worth emphasizing. Offer me a bar, offer me a gay bar, offer me a BDSM club. The person's personality doesn't matter, we're not in a place with music this loud to have a good talk; we want blood. Feed on site or take them home, it doesn't matter, the blood matters. A beautifully written, well crafted romantic narrative is going to take resources and isn't going to hit all players, but this? This is simple, and players understand what it means to the character more than they do a sappy romance that doesn't click for them. </div> </div> </div> </div>Romance is pretty. It brightens everyone\u2019s life. Even a vampire\u2019s. And even a fanatical Sabbat paladin who\u2019s totally devoted to the Sword of Caine finds her life pleasantly complicated on those rare occasions when she falls for someone (especially if that person is an enemy). Granted, this works best for tabletop RPGs and MMOs, but there\u2019s no reason it couldn\u2019t work for a game like Bloodlines too (Dragon Age did a great job with interpersonal relationships). A lot of players would probably like a romance angle instead of just making everything about hooking up in order to feed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T15:02:01-07:00","id":1407038,"title":"","content":"Touchstones might be worth including. Probably not mechanically, but there could be some human characters who are only connected to the kindred world through the PC. Like if you met Samantha multiple times in her own story.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, some hook ups do involve <i>a lot</i> of talking. I imagine it would be one of the main ways that some kindred connect to humans and humanity. It isn't always even verbal, but that kind of intimacy is difficult to portray in any medium. So blood dolls could be reasonably fleshed out characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer