nd ofc there is theeffects of a blood bond, so you could indeed find your &quot;love&quot; as a kainite amongst the kainites and for some reason start with a blood bond and that deepens, leadiong to what would become a real romance with evertything. The good part about this is, that you can have a vast pool of potential romance partners without it feeling forced. Gay, fetish, all kinds of personalities - the blood bond makes it work so the character doesnt even have to like their romance so the player is free to choose what they want to see.<br /> <br /> Personally, and i know thats the least likely event, id love a mix of all of these. How about we start the game as mortal and build a romance with an npc we like, then become a vampire, make that npc of choice our ghoul, really care for them, then later down the line they become a vampire themselves - maybe your child but maybe abducted and becoming a full vampire through someone else and you continue with a blood bond from there. Could be a great tool to show how the embrace changes people and maybe your lvoed one becomes someone you dont like but are blood bound too anyway<br /> <br /> And the idea about adding BDSM clubs to the game would be absolutely brilliant. It does not only fit the ghoul theme (and artbook) but there is such locations in official campains so why not ingame. That said making a woman whos already a / my sub into my ghoul feels way less abusive and actually something she could really enjoy. that would be my pick for romance XD<br /> However i doubt the studio has the balls to do that, and i can see the press about promoting abusive relationships, objectfiyng women...its what real life bdsm couples get all the time anyway.<br /> That said the opposite roles with a female dom and a male sub is priced and theres nothing stopping the game from having that an option as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":"