hing. The good part about this is, that you can have a vast pool of potential romance partners without it feeling forced. Gay, fetish, all kinds of personalities - the blood bond makes it work so the character doesnt even have to like their romance so the player is free to choose what they want to see.<br /> <br /> Personally, and i know thats the least likely event, id love a mix of all of these. How about we start the game as mortal and build a romance with an npc we like, then become a vampire, make that npc of choice our ghoul, really care for them, then later down the line they become a vampire themselves - maybe your child but maybe abducted and becoming a full vampire through someone else and you continue with a blood bond from there. Could be a great tool to show how the embrace changes people and maybe your lvoed one becomes someone you dont like but are blood bound too anyway<br /> <br /> And the idea about adding BDSM clubs to the game would be absolutely brilliant. It does not only fit the ghoul theme (and artbook) but there is such locations in official campains so why not ingame. That said making a woman whos already a / my sub into my ghoul feels way less abusive and actually something she could really enjoy. that would be my pick for romance XD<br /> However i doubt the studio has the balls to do that, and i can see the press about promoting abusive relationships, objectfiyng women...its what real life bdsm couples get all the time anyway.<br /> That said the opposite roles with a female dom and a male sub is priced and theres nothing stopping the game from having that an option as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point but I guess I don\u2019t see vampires as that different from humans who just need blood in order to survive. I guess it depends on what you as a player really like. If lush vivid romance and passionate makeout scenes don\u2019t do much for you irl, you\u2019re not gonna want them in your Vampire game either. I wouldn\u2019t want them to dominate the game (whether tabletop or video game), that would be too sickly sweet, but imo a little romance gives your character more flavor, makes their life richer and more full. I don\u2019t even play video games that much so I\u2019m probably not the target audience for Bloodlines, but I think there are other players like me who would like to see that as an option in their games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T04:53:30-07:00","id":1407119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1325367-do-you-think-that-bloodlines-was-in-any-way-a-sexist-game?p=1407083#post1407083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general idea of a romance in a vampires game is...difficult. Most vampires dont have such feelings and dont give a crap, also about sex which is a part of a romance and its also looked down upon by other kindred. Not to mention its a weakness added to your character that can be exploited by enemies (see heather)</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, vampires are intensely sexual beings. It's just that the blood is how the desire for sex manifests. Drinking is better than sex and drugs combined while being the sex and drugs that you have every night. Vampires who get naked with a partner and roll around with them while drinking are g